 is reasonably available and they are themselves an MP or AMHP. The extension is recorded in the approved form with the time granted, the new expiry and the reasons, and filed with a copy to the person. A referral cannot be extended more than once.","reviewStatus":"drafted"},{"section":"46","title":"Changing place where examination will be conducted","summary":"An MP or AMHP may change the place specified in a s 26 referral where the examination will be conducted, but only after consulting a practitioner at the proposed new place. They must promptly tell whoever is transporting the person, record the change in the approved form with the old and new places and the time, and file it with a copy to the person. Changing between an authorised hospital and a non-hospital place switches which limb of s 26 the referral is treated as having been made under.","reviewStatus":"drafted"}],"sourceFacts":{"documentTitle":"Variation Of Referral","fileName":"📋 Form 1B.pdf","pages":2,"timings":["72 hours"],"sectionCue":"sections 45, 46","indexedAt":"Official form PDF indexed locally"},"availability":"downloadable","officialPdfUrl":"https://www.chiefpsychiatrist.wa.gov.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/FORM1B_MHA2014__public.pdf","officialRegisterUrl":"https://www.chiefpsychiatrist.wa.gov.au/laws-and-rights/legislation/mental-health-act-2014-forms/","localPdfPath":"/forms-pdf/form-1b.pdf","localPdfSha256":"e29fab5a3747d39c59201671c1e8165cdce9fca0006501946196fb3f3c3c88ed","localPdfBytes":199390,"officialPdfPasswordProtected":true,"officialPdfEditingRestricted":true,"officialTitleCheckedAt":"17 July 2026","archiveGeneratedAt":"2026-07-13T16:02:29.961824Z"}},"form:form-2":{"slug":"form-2","title":"Order to detain voluntary inpatient in authorised hospital for assessment","subtitle":"Use for a voluntary inpatient requesting discharge where urgent assessment is required.","statusChips":[{"label":"high risk","tone":"danger"},{"label":"Referral and detention","tone":"info"},{"label":"Official PD