"label":"Documentation stem","value":"Voluntary inpatient requested discharge at [time]. Form 2 commenced because [assessment reason]. Expiry and next lawful step documented."},{"label":"Safety pearl","value":"The expiry is the clinical priority. Decide and document the next lawful step early."},{"label":"Common traps","value":"Missing the 6-hour hard stop. Static detention without active assessment. Not documenting release/off-ramp."},{"label":"Pre-use checks","value":"Before use: confirm live referral/order, detention place, expiry, receiving service and release/off-ramp trigger. Confirm the patient/person identifiers, maker, date, time, place and signature fields are complete. Confirm copies, notices, support-person communication and filing/PSOLIS requirements before handover. Open the official PDF when the form wording or authority boundary matters."}],"bestUse":"Detention authority must match the live referral or examination pathway, place, duration and expiry; do not use detention wording as treatment or transport authority. Use only the current approved form or PSOLIS pathway where available; only appropriately authorised people should complete MHA 2014 forms. Authority is limited to the Act sections, signature block, time limits and wording on the approved form.","criteria":[{"label":"Before use: confirm live referral/order, detention place, expiry, receiving service and release/off-ramp trigger.","tone":"caution"},{"label":"Confirm the patient/person identifiers, maker, date, time, place and signature fields are complete.","tone":"caution"},{"label":"Confirm copies, notices, support-person communication and filing/PSOLIS requirements before handover.","tone":"caution"},{"label":"Missing the 6-hour hard stop.","tone":"reject"},{"label":"Static detention without active assessment.","tone":"reject"}],"verification":{"locallyVerified":false,"confidence":"Medium","notes":["Official title and availability checked 17 July 2026","Archive guidance remains a prototype reference aid and requires local clinical/legal governance review","Use the current approved PDF or PSOLIS form; do not modify approved form content"]},"tags":["Form 2","Referral and detention","Mental Health Act 2014","voluntary inpatient","wants to leave","assessment hold","6 hours","expired","hard stop","leave ward","discharge"],"catchments":["Western Australia"],"catalogueLabel":"Form 2","navigatorQuery":"Form 2 Order to detain voluntary inpatient in authorised hospital for assessment Referral and detention Use for a voluntary inpatient requesting discharge where urgent assessment is required. 6 hours, up to 6 hours inpatient voluntary treatment assessment authorised hospital time detained 6 hours up to 6 hours","source":{"label":"Office of the Chief Psychiatrist WA — approved MHA 2014 forms","status":"Source checked","url":"https://www.chiefpsychiatrist.wa.gov.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/FORM2_MHA2014__public.pdf","reviewed":"Official register checked 17 July 2026","notes":["Open the official source to confirm the current approved version before use","PSOLIS is the preferred completion method where available"]},"catalogPayload":{"id":"form-2","form":"2","name":"Order to detain voluntary inpatient in authorised hospital for assessment","category":"Referral and detention","purpose":"Use for a voluntary inpatient requesting discharge where urgent assessment is required.","maker":"Authorised clinician specified by the Act pathway.","involved":"Ward medical team, nursing coordinator, psychiatrist or registrar.","threshold":"Assessment is required and no lawful next step has yet been completed.","clock":"Maximum 6 hours. Treat as a hard stop.","destination":"Adult inpatient ward or relevant hospital setting.","authorises":"Short assessment hold for the voluntary inpatient pathway.","doesNotAuthorise":"Ongoing detention beyond the maximum period or treatment without separate authority.","before":[],"parallel":["1A"],"after":["Release","1A","3A"],"copies":"Hand over expiry and next owner clearly.","documentationStem":"Voluntary inpatient requested discharge at [time]. Form 2 commenced because [assessment reason]. Expiry and next lawful step documented.","traps":["Missing the 6-hour hard stop.","Static detention without active assessment.","Not documenting release/off-ramp."],"safetyPearl":"The expiry is the clinical priority. Decide and document the next lawful step early.","sourceNote":"Representative summary from supplied forms guide.","aliases":["voluntary inpatient","wants to leave","assessment hold"],"searchTerms":["6 hours","expired","hard stop","leave ward","discharge"],"riskLevel":"high","indexedClock":"6 hours, up to 6 hours","indexedTerms":["inpatient","voluntary","treatment","assessment","authorised","hospital","time","detained","6 hours","up to 6 hours"],"legalNote":"Detention authority must match the live referral or examination pathway, place, duration and expiry; do not use detention wording as treatment or transport authority. Use only the current approved form or PSOLIS pathway where available; only appropriately authorised people should complete MHA 2014 forms. Authority is limited to the Act sections, signature block, time limits and wording on the approved form.","practicePearls":["The expiry is the clinical priority. Decide and document the next lawful step early.","The lawful clock and destination are the safety-critical parts of detention forms.","Clock cue: 6 hours, up to 6 hours. Record the start time, expiry or review point, and next owner.","Source cue: sections 34, 35."],"preUseChecks":["Before use: confirm live referral/order, detention place, expiry, receiving service and release/off-ramp trigger.","Confirm the patient/person identifiers, maker, date, time, place and signature fields are complete.","Confirm copies, notices, support-person communication and filing/PSOLIS requirements before handover.","Open the official PDF when the form wording or authority boundary matters."],"actSections":[{"section":"34","title":"Person in charge of ward may order assessment","summary":"Where a voluntary inpatient wants to leave against medical advice and the person in charge of the ward reasonably suspects, on the section 25 criteria, that they need an involuntary treatment order, that person may order an assessment by an MP or AMHP at the hospital. The inpatient can be detained for up to 6 hours to allow it. The order is in the approved form and is filed with a copy to the patient, and the inpatient must be given the opportunity and means to contact a support person, their treating health professional and the Chief Mental Health Advocate. Detention ends at 6 hours if the assessment is not completed, or is completed without a s 36(2) referral being made.","reviewStatus":"drafted"},{"section":"35","title":"Revoking order for assessment","summary":"The person who ordered a s 34 assessment may revoke that order at any time before the assessment starts, if satisfied the patient no longer needs an involuntary treatment order. The revocation is in the approved form and is filed with a copy to the patient, and detention cannot continue once it is made.","reviewStatus":"drafted"}],"sourceFacts":{"documentTitle":"Order To Detain Voluntary Inpatient In Authorised Hospital For Assessment","fileName":"📋 Form 2.pdf","pages":2,"timings":["6 hours","up to 6 hours"],"sectionCue":"sections 34, 35","indexedAt":"Official form PDF indexed locally"},"availability":"downloadable","officialPdfUrl":"https://www.chiefpsychiatrist.wa.gov.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/FORM2_MHA2014__public.pdf","officialRegisterUrl":"https://www.chiefpsychiatrist.wa.gov.au/laws-and-rights/legislation/mental-health-act-2014-forms/","localPdfPath":"/forms-pdf/form-2.pdf","localPdfSha256":"37a058026a6ad1fce0a080dc18ded26afc794836ffb590a2cbbba65087eec7bb","localPdfBytes":228235,"officialPdfPasswordProtected":true,"officialPdfEditingRestricted":true,"officialTitleCheckedAt":"17 July 2026","archiveGeneratedAt":"2026-07-13T16:02:29.961824Z"}},"form:detention-examination-movement":{"slug":"detention-examination-movement","title":"Detention order","subtitle":"Use where detention is required to enable a referred person to be taken to an examination place.","statusChips":[{"label":"high risk","tone":"danger"},{"label":"Referral and detention","tone":"info"},{"label":"Official PDF","tone":"success"}],"primaryContact":{"label":"Form code","value":"Form 3A","detail":"Official PDF","kind":"text"},"contacts":[{"label":"Official public PDF","value":"https://www.chiefpsychiatrist.wa.gov.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/FORM3A_MHA2014__public.pdf","detail":"Current OCP source","kind":"web"},{"label":"Official forms register","value":"https://www.chiefpsychiatrist.wa.gov.au/laws-and-rights/legislation/mental-health-act-2014-forms/","detail":"Check current availability","kind":"web"}],"route":"Before: 1A | Parallel: 4A | After: Psychiatrist examination, 3B","eligibility":"A live referral exists and detention is needed for the lawful examination pathway.","cost":"Official WA Mental Health Act 2014 form","referral":"Before use: confirm live referral/order, detention place, expiry, receiving service and release/off-ramp trigger.","location":"Western Australia","summaryCards":[{"id":"clock","label":"Clock / review","title":"24-hour blocks; cannot outlast the referral.","detail":"Up to 24 hours, 24 hours, 72 hours, 144 hours"},{"id":"authority","label":"Made by / authority","title":"Authorised person specified by the detention pathway.","detail":"Detention for the specified pre-examination pathway."},{"id":"criteria","label":"Criteria / threshold","title":"A live referral exists and detention is needed for the lawful examination pathway.","detail":"Transport by itself unless transport authority also exists."},{"id":"act-sections","label":"Act sections","title":"Authority under the Act","detail":"28"}],"referralInfo":[{"label":"Purpose","value":"Use where detention is required to enable a referred perso