-person communication and filing/PSOLIS requirements before handover.","tone":"caution"},{"label":"Detention clock outlasting referral.","tone":"reject"},{"label":"Using detention as transport authority.","tone":"reject"}],"verification":{"locallyVerified":false,"confidence":"Medium","notes":["Official title and availability checked 17 July 2026","Archive guidance remains a prototype reference aid and requires local clinical/legal governance review","Use the current approved PDF or PSOLIS form; do not modify approved form content"]},"tags":["Form 3A","Referral and detention","Mental Health Act 2014","detain before exam","pre exam detention","3a detention","transport","destination","expiry","referral","force"],"catchments":["Western Australia"],"catalogueLabel":"Form 3A","navigatorQuery":"Form 3A Detention order Referral and detention Use where detention is required to enable a referred person to be taken to an examination place. Up to 24 hours, 24 hours, 72 hours, 144 hours detention detained time practitioner made place psychiatrist hours Up to 24 hours 24 hours 72 hours 144 hours","source":{"label":"Office of the Chief Psychiatrist WA — approved MHA 2014 forms","status":"Source checked","url":"https://www.chiefpsychiatrist.wa.gov.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/FORM3A_MHA2014__public.pdf","reviewed":"Official register checked 17 July 2026","notes":["Open the official source to confirm the current approved version before use","PSOLIS is the preferred completion method where available"]},"catalogPayload":{"id":"form-3a","form":"3A","name":"Detention order","category":"Referral and detention","purpose":"Use where detention is required to enable a referred person to be taken to an examination place.","maker":"Authorised person specified by the detention pathway.","involved":"Referring clinician, transport team, receiving service.","threshold":"A live referral exists and detention is needed for the lawful examination pathway.","clock":"24-hour blocks; cannot outlast the 