hospital within 24 hours of admission under the transfer order. Confirmation requires examining the inpatient, and is recorded in the approved form with the time, the reasons and the psychiatrist's details. The inpatient treatment order ceases to be in force if it is not confirmed in time, and that release is a Part 9 notifiable event.","reviewStatus":"drafted"},{"section":"124","title":"Confirmation of inpatient treatment order","summary":"Where the supervising psychiatrist made an inpatient treatment order under s 120(2)(a) or 123(1)(a) without being in the patient's physical presence for the examination, and no in-person psychiatrist examination has happened since, the order must be confirmed by a psychiatrist at the authorised hospital within 24 hours of admission. Confirmation requires examining the patient, and is recorded in the approved form with the time, the reasons and the psychiatrist's details. The order ceases to be in force if it is not confirmed in time, and that release is a Part 9 notifiable event.","reviewStatus":"drafted"}],"sourceFacts":{"documentTitle":"Confirmation Of Inpatient Treatment Order","fileName":"📋 Form 6D.pdf","pages":2,"timings":["within 24 hours","within 24 hour"],"sectionCue":"sections 68, 124","indexedAt":"Official form PDF indexed locally"},"availability":"downloadable","officialPdfUrl":"https://www.chiefpsychiatrist.wa.gov.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/FORM6D_MHA2014__public.pdf","officialRegisterUrl":"https://www.chiefpsychiatrist.wa.gov.au/laws-and-rights/legislation/mental-health-act-2014-forms/","localPdfPath":"/forms-pdf/form-6d.pdf","localPdfSha256":"1255f29f95680ce991193e5b3d4115cf232d2fd6a88a277899fb628831f4a793","localPdfBytes":192551,"officialPdfPasswordProtected":true,"officialPdfEditingRestricted":true,"officialTitleCheckedAt":"17 July 2026","archiveGeneratedAt":"2026-07-13T16:02:29.961824Z"}},"form:form-7a":{"slug":"form-7a","title":"Grant of leave to involuntary inpatient","subtitle":"Use for each leave episode f