ecord must ensure it is filed and a copy given to the person searched.","reviewStatus":"drafted"},{"section":"166","title":"Dealing with articles seized when person apprehended","summary":"An article seized under s 159(2)(c) from someone apprehended must be given to the person in charge of the service or place when they are received there, or to the practitioner into whose care they are delivered, or returned to the person if they are released without being taken anywhere — or otherwise dealt with according to law. Whoever deals with the article must record the details in the approved form as soon as practicable and give that record to the same recipient, and a person in charge or practitioner receiving it must ensure it is filed.","reviewStatus":"drafted"}],"sourceFacts":{"documentTitle":"Record Of Search And Seizure","fileName":"📋 Form 8A.pdf","pages":2,"timings":["Check timing","expiry and review requirements in the source."],"sectionCue":"sections 165, 166","indexedAt":"Official form PDF indexed locally"},"availability":"downloadable","officialPdfUrl":"https://www.chiefpsychiatrist.wa.gov.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/FORM8A_MHA2014__public.pdf","officialRegisterUrl":"https://www.chiefpsychiatrist.wa.gov.au/laws-and-rights/legislation/mental-health-act-2014-forms/","localPdfPath":"/forms-pdf/form-8a.pdf","localPdfSha256":"6905abc6454d6fbf6ab6d075e538f0505e900d713861820d146c25d4d765e8da","localPdfBytes":233991,"officialPdfPasswordProtected":true,"officialPdfEditingRestricted":true,"officialTitleCheckedAt":"17 July 2026","archiveGeneratedAt":"2026-07-13T16:02:29.961824Z"}},"form:form-8b":{"slug":"form-8b","title":"Record dealing with seized article","subtitle":"Official form source: Record Of Dealing With Seized Article. Review the source snippets and approved form before use.","statusChips":[{"label":"medium risk","tone":"warning"},{"label":"Search and seizure","tone":"info"},{"label":"Official PDF","tone":"success"}],"primaryContact":{"label":"Form code","value"