r other personal support person, unless that is not appropriate. If neither happens at that point the article may be returned or handed over later, and otherwise must be stored and may be destroyed or disposed of after 6 months. A record of how the article was dealt with must be filed in the approved form, covering the details of the article, the dates it was returned or handed over, or the reasons it was not, and the date and manner of any destruction or disposal.","reviewStatus":"drafted"}],"sourceFacts":{"documentTitle":"Record Of Dealing With Seized Article","fileName":"📋 Form 8B.pdf","pages":2,"timings":["6 months"],"sectionCue":"sections 167","indexedAt":"Official form PDF indexed locally"},"availability":"downloadable","officialPdfUrl":"https://www.chiefpsychiatrist.wa.gov.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/FORM8B_MHA2014__public.pdf","officialRegisterUrl":"https://www.chiefpsychiatrist.wa.gov.au/laws-and-rights/legislation/mental-health-act-2014-forms/","localPdfPath":"/forms-pdf/form-8b.pdf","localPdfSha256":"36971415aac62a9d96ae4d1312d230eb8dede4bba71041597b2b3fae8eeccc7f","localPdfBytes":174112,"officialPdfPasswordProtected":true,"officialPdfEditingRestricted":true,"officialTitleCheckedAt":"17 July 2026","archiveGeneratedAt":"2026-07-13T16:02:29.961824Z"}},"form:form-9a":{"slug":"form-9a","title":"Record of emergency psychiatric treatment","subtitle":"Use where emergency psychiatric treatment without consent is required.","statusChips":[{"label":"high risk","tone":"danger"},{"label":"Treatments","tone":"info"},{"label":"Official PDF","tone":"success"}],"primaryContact":{"label":"Form code","value":"Form 9A","detail":"Official PDF","kind":"text"},"contacts":[{"label":"Official public PDF","value":"https://www.chiefpsychiatrist.wa.gov.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/FORM9A_MHA2014__public.pdf","detail":"Current OCP source","kind":"web"},{"label":"Official forms register","value":"https://www.chiefpsychiatrist.wa.gov.au/laws-and-rights/legislation/mental-health-act