ng whether, on the s 232(1) criteria, restraint should continue. If restraint lasts more than 6 hours a psychiatrist must review its use and record their name, qualifications and the date, time and results of the review. The person must be provided with appropriate bedding and clothing, sufficient food and drink, access to toilet facilities, and any other care appropriate to their needs.","reviewStatus":"drafted"}],"availability":"downloadable","officialPdfUrl":"https://www.chiefpsychiatrist.wa.gov.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/FORM10H_MHA2014__public.pdf","officialRegisterUrl":"https://www.chiefpsychiatrist.wa.gov.au/laws-and-rights/legislation/mental-health-act-2014-forms/","localPdfPath":"/forms-pdf/form-10h.pdf","localPdfSha256":"bcc7d65fc6ca21f12b9662b5ff51301f45c505d092f09507d96fc4fc7da65094","localPdfBytes":221265,"officialPdfPasswordProtected":true,"officialPdfEditingRestricted":true,"officialTitleCheckedAt":"17 July 2026","archiveGeneratedAt":"2026-07-13T16:02:29.961824Z"}},"form:form-10i":{"slug":"form-10i","title":"Record of post-bodily restraint examination","subtitle":"Official form source: Record Of Post-Bodily Restraint Examination. Review the source snippets and approved form before use.","statusChips":[{"label":"high risk","tone":"danger"},{"label":"Restraint","tone":"info"},{"label":"Official PDF","tone":"success"}],"primaryContact":{"label":"Form code","value":"Form 10I","detail":"Official PDF","kind":"text"},"contacts":[{"label":"Official public PDF","value":"https://www.chiefpsychiatrist.wa.gov.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/FORM10I_MHA2014__public.pdf","detail":"Current OCP source","kind":"web"},{"label":"Official forms register","value":"https://www.chiefpsychiatrist.wa.gov.au/laws-and-rights/legislation/mental-health-act-2014-forms/","detail":"Check current availability","kind":"web"}],"route":"Confirm the current approved form pathway and local policy.","eligibility":"Use the threshold stated in the official form and any linked guidance.","co