uthority, person/place/items, handling of seized property and required records or notices. Use only the current approved form or PSOLIS pathway where available; only appropriately authorised people should complete MHA 2014 forms. Authority is limited to the Act sections, signature block, time limits and wording on the approved form.","practicePearls":["Open the source snippets before relying on the pathway.","Make the item trail auditable: reason, search scope, seizure, storage, return or disposal.","Clock cue: within 6 hours. Record the start time, expiry or review point, and next owner.","Source cue: sections 239."],"preUseChecks":["Before use: confirm search basis, scope, witnesses/supports, item handling, receipts/notices and filing.","Confirm the patient/person identifiers, maker, date, time, place and signature fields are complete.","Confirm copies, notices, support-person communication and filing/PSOLIS requirements before handover.","Open the official PDF when the form wording or authority boundary matters."],"actSections":[{"section":"239","title":"Examination of person when released","summary":"Whenever a person is released from bodily restraint, the person in charge of the ward must ensure they are examined by a medical practitioner as soon as practicable and in any event within 6 hours — or, if they are to be released or discharged or want to leave against medical advice before that, that an examination is offered beforehand. The examining practitioner must record their name and qualifications, the time of the examination, and the results, including any complication of or deterioration in the person's mental or physical condition that is or may be a result of the restraint, then file it with a copy to the person.","reviewStatus":"drafted"}],"sourceFacts":{"documentTitle":"Record Of Post-Bodily Restraint Examination","fileName":"📋 Form 10I.pdf","pages":2,"timings":["within 6 hours"],"sectionCue":"sections 239","indexedAt":"Official form PDF indexed locally"},"availability":"downloadable","officialPdfUrl":"https://www.chiefpsychiatrist.wa.gov.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/FORM10I_MHA2014__public.pdf","officialRegisterUrl":"https://www.chiefpsychiatrist.wa.gov.au/laws-and-rights/legislation/mental-health-act-2014-forms/","localPdfPath":"/forms-pdf/form-10i.pdf","localPdfSha256":"9bbb3bfd4103ffa811fa60456bc61cf66dc3b0f51468ff9b896758376c502811","localPdfBytes":234932,"officialPdfPasswordProtected":true,"officialPdfEditingRestricted":true,"officialTitleCheckedAt":"17 July 2026","archiveGeneratedAt":"2026-07-13T16:02:29.961824Z"}},"form:form-11a":{"slug":"form-11a","title":"Record of oral authorisation of seclusion","subtitle":"Use for seclusion episode documentation and authorisation pathway.","statusChips":[{"label":"high risk","tone":"danger"},{"label":"Seclusion","tone":"info"},{"label":"Official PDF","tone":"success"}],"primaryContact":{"label":"Form code","value":"Form 11A","detail":"Official PDF","kind":"text"},"contacts":[{"label":"Official public PDF","value":"https://www.chiefpsychiatrist.wa.gov.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/FORM11A_MHA2014__public.pdf","detail":"Current OCP source","kind":"web"},{"label":"Official forms register","value":"https://www.chiefpsychiatrist.wa.gov.au/laws-and-rights/legislation/mental-health-act-2014-forms/","detail":"Check current availability","kind":"web"}],"route":"Before: Clinical de-escalation | Parallel: 11B, 11G | After: Release, review, debrief","eligibility":"Seclusion is required and no less restrictive option is sufficient.","cost":"Official WA Mental Health Act 2014 form","referral":"Before use: confirm reason, start time, written confirmation deadline, observation plan, review and post-event examination.","location":"Western Australia","summaryCards":[{"id":"clock","label":"Clock / review","title":"Oral to written order within 2 hours; ongoing review requirements apply.","detail":"within 2 hours"},{"id":"authority","label":"Made by / authority","title":"Authorised clinician according to seclusion pathway.","detail":"Seclusion episode according to the order."},{"id":"criteria","label":"Criteria / threshold","title":"Seclusion is required and no less restrictive option is sufficient.","detail":"Bodily restraint or indefinite seclusion without review."},{"id":"act-sections","label":"Act sections","title":"Authority under the Act","detail":"214"}],"referralInfo":[{"label":"Purpose","value":"Use for seclusion episode documentation and authorisation pathway."},{"label":"Authorises","value":"Seclusion episode according to the order."},{"label":"Does not authorise","value":"Bodily restraint or indefinite seclusion without review."},{"label":"Before","value":"Clinical de-escalation"},{"label":"Parallel","value":"11B, 11G"},{"label":"After","value":"Release, review, debrief"},{"label":"Copies and filing","value":"Observation, order and review records as required."},{"label":"Documentation stem","value":"Seclusion authorised at [time] because [reason], less restrictive options insufficient, observation/review plan documented."},{"label":"Safety pearl","value":"Seclusion has its own clock and review pathway."},{"label":"Common traps","value":"Missing written order timing. Review not diarised. Confusing seclusion with restraint pathway."},{"label":"Pre-use checks","value":"Before use: confirm reason, start time, written confirmation deadline, observation plan, review and post-event examination. Confirm the patient/person identifiers, maker, date, time, place and signature fields are complete. Confirm copies, notices, support-person communication and filing/PSOLIS requirements before handover. Open the official PDF when the form wording or authority boundary matters."}],"bestUse":"Restrictive-practice forms should be episode-specific and show reason, least restrictive alternatives, observation, review and post-event checks. Use only the current approved form or PSOLIS pathway where available; only appropriately authorised people should complete MHA 2014 forms. Authority is limited to the Act sections, signature block, time limits and wording on the approved form.","criteria":[{"label":"Before use: confirm reason, start time, written confirmation deadline, observation plan, review and post-event examination.","tone":"caution"},{"label":"Confirm the patient/person identifiers, maker, date, time, place and signature fields are complete.","tone":"caution"},{"label":"Confirm copies, notices, support-person communication and filing/PSOLIS requirements before handover.","tone":"caution"},{"label":"Missing written order timing.","tone":"reject"},{"label":"Review not diarised.","tone":"reject"}],"verification":{"locallyVerified":false,"confidence":"Medium","notes":["Official title and availability checked 17 July 2026","Archive guidance remains a prototype reference aid and requires local clinical/legal governance review","Use the current approved PDF or PSOLIS form; do not modify approved form content"]},"tags":["Form 11A","Seclusion","Mental Health Act 2014","seclusion","11a","restrictive practice","2 hours","review","observation","restrictive"],"catchments":["Western Australia"],"catalogueLabel":"Form 11A","navigatorQuery":"Form 11A Record of oral authorisation of seclusion Seclusion Use for seclusion episode documentation and authorisation pathway. within 2 hours seclusion authorised oral authorisation hospital secluded record psychiatrist within 2 hours","source":{"label":"Office of the Chief Psychiatrist WA — approved MHA 2014 forms","status":"Source checked","url":"https://www.chiefpsychiatrist.wa.gov.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/FORM11A_MHA2014__public.pdf","reviewed":"Official register checked 17 July 2026","notes":["Open the official source to confirm the current approved version before use","PSOLIS is the preferred completion method where available"]},"catalogPayload":{"id":"form-11a","form":"11A","name":"Record of oral authorisation of seclusion","category":"Seclusion","purpose":"Use for seclusion episode documentation and authorisation pathway.","maker":"Authorised clinician according to seclusion pathway.","involved":"Nursing team, medical practitioner, observer, reviewer.","threshold":"Seclusion is required and no less restrictive option is sufficient.","clock":"Oral to written order within 2 hours; ongoing review requirements apply.","destination":"Seclusion area with observation requirements.","authorises":"Seclusion episode according to the order.","doesNotAuthorise":"Bodily restraint or indefinite seclusion without review.","before":["Clinical de-escalation"],"parallel":["11B","11G"],"after":["Release","review","debrief"],"copies":"Observation, order and review records as required.","documentationStem":"Seclusion authorised at [time] because [reason], less restrictive options insufficient, observation/review plan documented.","traps":["Missing written order timing.","Review not diarised.","Confusing seclusion with restraint pathway."],"safetyPearl":"Seclusion has its own clock and review pathway.","sourceNote":"Representative summary from supplied forms guide.","aliases":["seclusion","11a","restrictive practice"],"searchTerms":["2 hours","review","observation","restrictive"],"riskLevel":"high","indexedClock":"within 2 hours","indexedTerms":["seclusion","authorised","oral","authorisation","hospital","secluded","record","psychiatrist","within 2 hours"],"legalNote":"Restrictive-practice forms should be episode-specific and show reason, least restrictive alternatives, observation, review and post-event checks. Use only the current approved form or PSOLIS pathway where available; only appropriately authorised people should complete MHA 2014 forms. Authority is limited to the Act sections, signature block, time limits and wording on the approved form.","practicePearls":["Seclusion has its own clock and review pathway.","The order, observation record and post-event review are one safety workflow.","Clock cue: within 2 hours. Record the start time, expiry or review point, and next owner.","Source cue: sections 214."],"preUseChecks":["Before use: confirm reason, start time, written confirmation deadline, observation plan, review and post-event examination.","Confirm the patient/person identifiers, maker, date, time, place and signature fields are complete.","Confirm copies, notices, support-person communication and filing/PSOLIS requirements before handover.","Open the official PDF when the form wording or authority boundary matters."],"actSections":[{"section":"214","title":"Giving oral authorisation","summary":"A medical practitioner or mental health practitioner at an authorised hospital, or the person in charge of a ward, may orally authorise seclusion of an admitted patient, a person referred under s 26(2) or 36(2) for examination there, or a person under a s 55(1)(c) or 61(1)(c) order — but only if satisfied of the s 216 matters, and they must specify the room or area. As soon as practicable after the person is secluded the authorisation is recorded in the approved form with the time given, the room or area and the reasons, and filed with a copy to the person. A mental health practitioner or person in charge of a ward must also inform a medical practitioner whether the person is or was secluded, in time for the examinations s 222(4) or 223(2) require, and record that. If a seclusion order confirming the oral authorisation is not made within 2 hours of the person being secluded, seclusion cannot continue and the person must be informed and released.","reviewStatus":"drafted"}],"sourceFacts":{"documentTitle":"Record Of Oral Authorisation Of Seclusion","fileName":"📋 Form 11A.pdf","pages":2,"timings":["within 2 hours"],"sectionCue":"sections 214","indexedAt":"Official form PDF indexed locally"},"availability":"downloadable","officialPdfUrl":"https://www.chiefpsychiatrist.wa.gov.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/FORM11A_MHA2014__public.pdf","officialRegisterUrl":"https://www.chiefpsychiatrist.wa.gov.au/laws-and-rights/legislation/mental-health-act-2014-forms/","localPdfPath":"/forms-pdf/form-11a.pdf","localPdfSha256":"c28e1a51deba8522965b0f95735624d8d016dce97f7a64e44c8fb489d8259dd6","localPdfBytes":279831,"officialPdfPasswordProtected":true,"officialPdfEditingRestricted":true,"officialTitleCheckedAt":"17 July 2026","archiveGeneratedAt":"2026-07-13T16:02:29.961824Z"}},"form:form-11b":{"slug":"form-11b","title":"Written seclusion order","subtitle":"Official form source: Written Seclusion Order. Review the source snippets and approved form before use.","statusChips":[{"label":"high risk","tone":"danger"},{"label":"Seclusion","tone":"info"},{"label":"Official PDF","tone":"success"}],"primaryContact":{"label":"Form code","value":"Form 11B","detail":"Official PDF","kind":"text"},"contacts":[{"label":"Official public PDF","value":"https://www.chiefpsychiatrist.wa.gov.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/FORM11B_MHA2014__public.pdf","detail":"Current OCP source","kind":"web"},{"label":"Official forms register","value":"https://www.chiefpsychiatrist.wa.gov.au/laws-and-rights/legislation/mental-health-act-2014-forms/","detail":"Check current availability","kind":"web"}],"route":"Confirm the current approved form pathway and local policy.","eligibility":"Use the threshold stated in the official form and any linked guidance.","cost":"Official WA Mental Health Act 2014 form","referral":"Before use: confirm reason, start time, written confirmation deadline, observation plan, review and post-event examination.","location":"Western Australia","summaryCards":[{"id":"clock","label":"Clock / review","title":"2 hours, within 2 hours"},{"id":"authority","label":"Made by / authority","title":"Check the official form signature block and Act sections.","detail":"Authority is limited to what the approved form and Act section state."},{"id":"criteria","label":"Criteria / threshold","title":"Use the threshold stated in the official form and any linked guidance.","detail":"Does not replace linked forms, consent, notificat