e approved form.","practicePearls":["Open the source snippets before relying on the pathway.","The order, observation record and post-event review are one safety workflow.","Clock cue: within 2 hours, 2 hours. Record the start time, expiry or review point, and next owner.","Source cue: sections 218, 222."],"preUseChecks":["Before use: confirm reason, start time, written confirmation deadline, observation plan, review and post-event examination.","Confirm the patient/person identifiers, maker, date, time, place and signature fields are complete.","Confirm copies, notices, support-person communication and filing/PSOLIS requirements before handover.","Open the official PDF when the form wording or authority boundary matters."],"actSections":[{"section":"218","title":"Extending seclusion order","summary":"A medical practitioner may extend a seclusion order in force for a further period of up to 2 hours. They cannot do so unless, immediately beforehand, they examine the person in accordance with s 222(4). The order must be filed as soon as practicable with a copy to the person.","reviewStatus":"drafted"},{"section":"222","title":"Requirements relating to seclusion","summary":"While a person is secluded, the person in charge of the ward must ensure these requirements are met. A mental health practitioner or nurse must observe the person every 15 minutes and file a record of those observations in the approved form with a copy to the person. A medical practitioner must examine the person at least every 2 hours and record their name and qualifications, the time of the examination, and the results — including whether, on the s 216(1) criteria, seclusion should continue — then file it with a copy to the person. The person must be provided with appropriate bedding and clothing, sufficient food and drink, access to toilet facilities, and any other care appropriate to their needs.","reviewStatus":"drafted"}],"sourceFacts":{"documentTitle":"Record Of Examination Of Secluded Person","fileName":"📋 Form 11E.pdf","pages":2,"timings":["within 2 hours","2 hours"],"sectionCue":"sections 218, 222","indexedAt":"Official form PDF indexed locally"},"availability":"downloadable","officialPdfUrl":"https://www.chiefpsychiatrist.wa.gov.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/FORM11E_MHA2014__public.pdf","officialRegisterUrl":"https://www.chiefpsychiatrist.wa.gov.au/laws-and-rights/legislation/mental-health-act-2014-forms/","localPdfPath":"/forms-pdf/form-11e.pdf","localPdfSha256":"0ede01108377a296062de71da2acaf92c8b98464e0ca68c523c677aeab9b88d3","localPdfBytes":236247,"officialPdfPasswordProtected":true,"officialPdfEditingRestricted":true,"officialTitleCheckedAt":"17 July 2026","archiveGeneratedAt":"2026-07-13T16:02:29.961824Z"}},"form:form-11f":{"slug":"form-11f","title":"Revocation or expiry of seclusion order","subtitle":"Official form source: Revocation Or Expiry Of Seclusion. Review the source snippets and approved form before use.","statusChips":[{"label":"medium risk","tone":"warning"},{"label":"Seclusion","tone":"info"},{"label":"Official PDF","tone":"success"}],"primaryContact":{"label":"Form code","value":"Form 11F","detail":"Official PDF","kind":"text"},"contacts":[{"label":"Official public PDF","value":"https://www.chiefpsychiatrist.wa.gov.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/FORM11F_MHA2014__public.pdf","detail":"Current OCP source","kind":"web"},{"label":"Official forms register","value":"https://www.chiefpsychiatrist.wa.gov.au/laws-and-rights/legislation/mental-health-act-2014-forms/","detail":"Check current availability","kind":"web"}],"route":"Confirm the current approved form pathway and local policy.","eligibility":"Use the threshold stated in the official form and any linked guidance.","cost":"Official WA Mental Health Act 2014 form","referral":"Before use: confirm reason, start time, written confirmation deadline, observation plan, review and post-event examination.","location":"Western Australia","summaryCards":[{"id":"clock","label":"Clock / review",