 support-person communication and filing/PSOLIS requirements before handover.","Open the official PDF when the form wording or authority boundary matters."],"actSections":[{"section":"248","title":"Right to access medical record and other documents","summary":"Unless s 249(1)(a) or (b) or (3) applies, a person who is or was provided with treatment or care by a mental health service is entitled to inspect and be given a copy of any relevant document about them held by the person in charge or a staff member, in addition to any other right of access they have. The person in charge must ensure any such request is dealt with as soon as practicable, and that if it is refused a record of the reasons is filed in the approved form and a copy given to the person.","reviewStatus":"drafted"}],"sourceFacts":{"documentTitle":"Record Of Refusal Of Patient's Request To Access Document","fileName":"📋 Form 12B.pdf","pages":2,"timings":["Check timing","expiry and review requirements in the source."],"sectionCue":"sections 248","indexedAt":"Official form PDF indexed locally"},"availability":"downloadable","officialPdfUrl":"https://www.chiefpsychiatrist.wa.gov.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/FORM12B_MHA2014__public.pdf","officialRegisterUrl":"https://www.chiefpsychiatrist.wa.gov.au/laws-and-rights/legislation/mental-health-act-2014-forms/","localPdfPath":"/forms-pdf/form-12b.pdf","localPdfSha256":"9deee79f80c652b7a4bdbc34643144d429c29520e42d971a5d78c2008bed79b0","localPdfBytes":236674,"officialPdfPasswordProtected":true,"officialPdfEditingRestricted":true,"officialTitleCheckedAt":"17 July 2026","archiveGeneratedAt":"2026-07-13T16:02:29.961824Z"}},"form:form-12c":{"slug":"form-12c","title":"Restriction on freedom of communication","subtitle":"Use when a communication right is restricted and review/notification requirements apply.","statusChips":[{"label":"high risk","tone":"danger"},{"label":"Access to information and communication","tone":"info"},{"label":"Official PDF","tone":"success"}]