. hyperthermia rising ck why it fits rigidity hyperthermia diaphoresis autonomic instability recent antipsychotic start/increase rigidity fever autonomic instability confusion after dopamine blockade or withdrawal temporal association with antipsychotic initiation dose change or depot timing. rigidity hyperthermia diaphoresis autonomic instability recent antipsychotic start/increase characteristic motor syndrome rather than simple low mood psychosis or behavioural refusal . mood disorders are a very common substrate. must-not-miss hyperthermia rising ck aki collapse severe autonomic instability. rhabdomyolysis aki collapse death. hyperthermia rising ck severe autonomic instability. bedside question characteristic motor syndrome rather than simple low mood psychosis or behavioural refusal . mood disorders are a very common substrate. temporal association with antipsychotic initiation dose change or depot timing. characteristic motor syndrome rather than simple low mood psychosis or behavioural refusal . mood disorders are a very common substrate. immediate action constipation with clozapine is a red flag not a nuisance side effect clozapine constipation and myocarditis are high-risk problems escalate early review bowels deliberately maintain active surveillance during early titration early activation is a common misread clinical toxicity can occur even when history suggests a usual dose check ammonia if unexplained confusion develops on valproate constipation with clozapine is a red flag not a nuisance side effect clozapine constipation and myocarditis are high-risk problems escalate early review bowels deliberately maintain active surveillance during early titration early activation is a common misread clinical toxicity can occur even when history suggests a usual dose check ammonia if unexplained confusion develops on valproate use structured screen bush-francis examine motor signs check vitals/hydration/ck think benzodiazepine challenge early catatonia is more oft