simism.\nTags: Severe dissociation, poor recall, aggressive defensive state, co-occurring substance use.\nptsd ptsd-dissociation-linked-risk trauma cues flashbacks dissociative states sustained wish to die or escape often with cognitive constriction and pessimism. severe dissociation poor recall aggressive defensive state co-occurring substance use. severe dissociation poor recall aggressive defensive state co-occurring substance use. why it fits trauma cues flashbacks dissociative states trauma cues flashbacks dissociative states sustained wish to die or escape often with cognitive constriction and pessimism. must-not-miss severe dissociation poor recall aggressive defensive state co-occurring substance use. severe dissociation poor recall aggressive defensive state co-occurring substance use. bedside question sustained wish to die or escape often with cognitive constriction and pessimism. sustained wish to die or escape often with cognitive constriction and pessimism. immediate action quiet organised suicidality is often higher risk than dramatic expression mixed states are easy to miss and carry very high suicide risk ask about content controllability and compliance not just presence of voices do not dismiss recurrent self-harm as low risk focus on intent lethality acute change dissociation substance use dissociated acts can be impulsive yet highly dangerous quiet organised suicidality is often higher risk than dramatic expression mixed states are easy to miss and carry very high suicide risk ask about content controllability and compliance not just presence of voices do not dismiss recurrent self-harm as low risk focus on intent lethality acute change dissociation substance use dissociated acts can be impulsive yet highly dangerous investigations mimics / overlap major depressive disorder hopelessness anhedonia guilt burdensomeness bipolar depression depression with agitation irritability racing thoughts psychosis-driven suicidality command hallucinations delusi