,"extension","officer","practitioner","date","time","place","expire","72 hours"],"riskLevel":"high","indexedTerms":[],"legalNote":"Transport or transfer authority should be specific to the journey, destination and linked live authority, with no safer less restrictive option available. Use only the current approved form or PSOLIS pathway where available; only appropriately authorised people should complete MHA 2014 forms. Authority is limited to the Act sections, signature block, time limits and wording on the approved form.","practicePearls":["Open the source snippets before relying on the pathway.","A transport form should make the route, destination and linked authority easy to audit.","Clock cue: 72 hours. Record the start time, expiry or review point, and next owner.","Source cue: sections 152."],"preUseChecks":["Before use: confirm origin, destination, transport provider, linked form, expiry and less restrictive travel options.","Confirm the patient/person identifiers, maker, date, time, place and signature fields are complete.","Confirm copies, notices, support-person communication and filing/PSOLIS requirements before handover.","Open the official PDF when the form wording or authority boundary matters."],"actSections":[{"section":"152","title":"Extension of other transport orders","summary":"Where a transport order made under s 63, 67, 92, 112, 129 or 133 is being carried out from a place outside the metropolitan area and the officer transporting the person forms the view it will expire before arrival, they may orally request an extension from a medical practitioner or mental health practitioner. The practitioner may orally make an extension order for a further period of up to 72 hours. They must then record it in the approved form with the time made and the new expiry, and file it with a copy to the officer. A transport order cannot be extended more than once.","reviewStatus":"drafted"}],"sourceFacts":{"documentTitle":"Extension Of Transport Order","fileName":"📋 Form 4B.pdf","pages":2,"timings":["72 hours"],"sectionCue":"sections 152","indexedAt":"Official form PDF indexed locally"},"availability":"downloadable","officialPdfUrl":"https://www.chiefpsychiatrist.wa.gov.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/FORM4B_MHA2014__public.pdf","officialRegisterUrl":"https://www.chiefpsychiatrist.wa.gov.au/laws-and-rights/legislation/mental-health-act-2014-forms/","localPdfPath":"/forms-pdf/form-4b.pdf","localPdfSha256":"e23a6be0f49f6e229d4c68212edb7a75baf99f47513a3061ad3d394e5175507e","localPdfBytes":179522,"officialPdfPasswordProtected":true,"officialTitleCheckedAt":"17 July 2026","archiveGeneratedAt":"2026-07-13T16:02:29.961824Z"}}},{"logicalId":"forms:form-10a","logicalDocumentId":"0def6c55-2ba9-506d-8330-1c4af9c97f97","logicalChunkId":"3e0ef361-9788-591f-b646-455823b77156","normalizedText":"Form: Record of oral authorisation of bodily restraint\nUse for bodily restraint episode documentation and authorisation pathway.\nRoute: Before: Clinical de-escalation | Parallel: 10B, 10I | After: Release, post-restraint examination, debrief\nEligibility: Required for treatment, preventing injury, or preventing serious property damage where no less restrictive way is available.\nReferral: Before use: confirm reason, start time, written confirmation deadline, observation plan, review and post-event examination.\nLocation: Western Australia\nBest use: Restrictive-practice forms should be episode-specific and show reason, least restrictive alternatives, observation, review and post-event checks. Use only the current approved form or PSOLIS pathway where available; only appropriately authorised people should complete MHA 2014 forms. Authority is limited to the Act sections, signature block, time limits and wording on the approved form.\nPrimary contact: Form 10A Official PDF\nTags: Form 10A, Restraint, Mental Health Act 2014, restraint, bodily restraint, 10a, restrictive practice, 30 minutes, force, injury, examination, 6 hours\nCatchments: Western Australia\nrecord of oral authorisation of bodily restraint form-10a use for bodily restraint episode documentation and authorisation pathway. before clinical de-escalation parallel 10b 10i after release post-restraint examination debrief required for treatment preventing injury or preventing serious property damage where no less restrictive way is available. official wa mental health act 2014 form before use confirm reason start time written confirmation deadline observation plan review and post-event examination. western australia restrictive-practice forms should be episode-specific and show reason least restrictive alternatives observation review and post-event checks. use only the current approved form or psolis pathway where available only appropriately authorised people should complete mha 2014 forms. authority is limited to the act sections signature block time limits and wording on the approved form. form 10a form 10a record of oral authorisation of bodily restraint restraint use for bodily restraint episode documentation and authorisation pathway. within 30 minutes restraint bodily oral authorisation authorised hospital record physical within 30 minutes form 10a official pdf office of the chief psychiatrist wa approved mha 2014 forms source checked official register checked 17 july 2026 form 10a restraint mental health act 2014 restraint bodily restraint 10a restrictive practice 30 minutes force injury examination 6 hours western australia high risk restraint official pdf official public pdf https //www.chiefpsychiatrist.wa.gov.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/form10a mha2014 public.pdf current ocp source official forms register https //www.chiefpsychiatrist.wa.gov.au/laws-and-rights/legislation/mental-health-act-2014-forms/ check current availability clock / review oral to written order within 30 minutes post-restraint examination within required window where applicable. within 30 minutes made by / authority authorised clinician according to restraint pathway. bodily restraint episode according to the order. criteria / threshold required for treatment preventing injury or preventing serious property damage where no less restrictive way is available. seclusion or ongoing restraint without review/order requirements. act sections authority under the act 230 purpose use for bodily restraint episode documentation and authorisation pathway. authorises bodily restraint episode according to the order. does not authorise seclusion or ongoing restraint without review/order requirements. before clinical de-escalation parallel 10b 10i after release post-restraint examination debrief copies and filing observation release injury and examination records as required. documentation stem bodily restraint authorised at time because reason no less restrictive option sufficient physical-health risk considered. safety pearl restrictive practice documentation is a clocked safety workflow not just an event note. common traps missing written confirmation timing. no post-release examination or aftercare check. pre-use checks before use confirm reason start time written confirmation deadline observation plan review and post-event examination. confirm the patient/person identifiers maker date time place and signature fields are complete. confirm copies notices support-person communication and filing/psolis requirements before handover. open the official pdf when the form wording or authority boundary matters. before use confirm reason start time written confirmation deadline observation plan review and post-event examination. caution confirm the patient/person identifiers maker date time place and signature fields are complete. caution confirm copies notices support-person communication and filing/psolis requirements before handover. caution missing written confirmation timing. reject no post-release examination or aftercare check. reject official title and availability checked 17 july 2026 archive guidance remains a prototype reference aid and requires local clinical/legal governance review use the current approved pdf or psolis form do not modify approved form content 10a restraint use for bodily restraint episode documentation and authorisation pathway. authorised clinician according to restraint pathway. required for treatment preventing injury or preventing serious property damage where no less restrictive way is available. oral to written order within 30 minutes post-restraint examination within required window where applicable. bodily restraint episode according to the order. seclusion or ongoing restraint without review/order requirements. restraint bodily restraint 10a restrictive practice 30 minutes force injury examination 6 hours restraint bodily oral authorisation authorised hospital record physical within 30 minutes section 230 giving oral authorisation a medical practitioner or mental health practitioner at an authorised hospital or the person in charge of a ward may orally authorise bodily restraint of an admitted patient a person referred under s 26 2 or 36 2 for examination there or a person under a s 55 1 c or 61 1 c order but only if satisfied of the s 232 matters. they must specify whether physical or mechanical restraint may be used and for mechanical restraint the device and how it may be applied to the person s body. as soon as practicable after the person is restrained the authorisation is recorded in the approved form with the time given those specifications and the reasons and filed with a copy to the person. a mental health practitioner or person in charge of a ward must also inform a medical practitioner whether the person is or was restrained in time for the examinations s 238 4 or 239 2 a require and record that. if a bodily restraint order confirming the oral authorisation is not made within 30 minutes of the person being restrained restraint cannot continue and the person must be informed and released. form forms checklist assessment transfer template","contentHash":"df1e8916