274 . official wa mental health act 2014 form confirm the person understands the effect of making the nomination s273 . western australia nomination under mha 2014 s273-s278 gives the nominated person statutory rights to information and involvement in treatment planning under s266 and rights advocacy under s263 subject to psychiatrist best-interests determination. it does not confer substitute decision-making guardianship or consent authority. valid until revoked by any means or resigned in writing. form 12a form 12a nomination of nominated person access to information and communication nomination of an adult nominated person under the mental health act 2014 to assist with rights receive treatment and care information and be involved in care planning. form 12a official pdf office of the chief psychiatrist wa approved mha 2014 forms source checked official register checked 17 july 2026 form 12a access to information and communication mental health act 2014 12a nomination of nominated person rights and notifications nominated person nomination s275 s273 s274 s276 s277 s278 rights involvement advocacy 18 years western australia medium risk access to information and communication official pdf official public pdf https //www.chiefpsychiatrist.wa.gov.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/form12a mha2014 public.pdf current ocp source official forms register https //www.chiefpsychiatrist.wa.gov.au/laws-and-rights/legislation/mental-health-act-2014-forms/ check current availability clock / review valid until revoked or resigned revocable at any time nominee must be 18+ made by / authority person understanding effect any age incl. child witnessed by authorised declaration taker nominee adult 18+ criteria / threshold person understands effect of nomination s273 max 1 nominee rights wishes treatment info involvement s263 s266 act sections authority under the act 275 purpose nomination of an adult nominated person under the mental health act 2014 to assist with rights receive treatment and care information and be involved in care planning. authorises authorises nominated person to be provided with information relating to treatment care rights and involuntary status and to be involved in matters relating to treatment and care planning s266 and ensure rights and wishes are observed s263 so long as the psychiatrist believes this is in the patient s best interests. does not authorise does not authorise the nominated person to consent to or refuse treatment on the patient s behalf make clinical decisions or act as an enduring guardian. copies and filing provide copy to nominated person file original in medical record and record in psolis / clinical information system. documentation stem nomination of nominated person completed on date . maker name understands effect . nominated person name adult 18+ . witnessed by authorised witness name/qualification . scope information sharing and care involvement under s263/s266. safety pearl a nominated person has rights to information and involvement under s266 but cannot consent to or refuse treatment on the patient s behalf. common traps treating the nominated person as having proxy consent or decision-making power over treatment. allowing the maker or nominated person to witness the nomination. nominating a minor under 18 years of age or having more than one active nominated person. pre-use checks confirm the person understands the effect of making the nomination s273 . confirm the nominated person is an adult aged 18 or over and has signed the acceptance block. confirm both maker and nominee signatures are witnessed by an authorised declaration taker who is neither maker nor nominee. confirm there is no existing active nomination a new nomination revokes prior ones under s277 . file in medical record and notify the treating team. confirm the person understands the effect of making the nomination s273 . caution confirm the nominated person is an adult aged 18 or over and has signed the acceptance block. caution