gatorQuery":"Form 1B Variation of referral Referral and detention Use to vary referral details or extend a referral where the non-metropolitan pathway applies. 72 hours referral place practitioner examination authorised medical time date 72 hours","source":{"label":"Office of the Chief Psychiatrist WA — approved MHA 2014 forms","status":"Source checked","url":"https://www.chiefpsychiatrist.wa.gov.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/FORM1B_MHA2014__public.pdf","reviewed":"Official register checked 17 July 2026","notes":["Open the official source to confirm the current approved version before use","PSOLIS is the preferred completion method where available"]},"catalogPayload":{"id":"form-1b","form":"1B","name":"Variation of referral","category":"Referral and detention","purpose":"Use to vary referral details or extend a referral where the non-metropolitan pathway applies.","maker":"Authorised maker specified by the form pathway.","involved":"Receiving hospital, transport lead, referring team.","threshold":"Existing referral remains live and variation or extension criteria are met.","clock":"Extension must be actioned before referral expiry where applicable.","destination":"Updated destination must be visible to the receiving team.","authorises":"Variation or extension of the referral pathway as specified.","doesNotAuthorise":"A new detention or transport power by itself.","before":["1A"],"parallel":["4B"],"after":["Psychiatrist examination"],"copies":"Update receiving service and records with changed referral details.","documentationStem":"Existing referral reviewed at [time]. Variation/extension required because [reason]. Updated destination/expiry: [details].","traps":["Assuming a variation fixes an expired referral.","Forgetting to update destination or receiving team."],"safetyPearl":"Variation is only useful while the underlying pathway is still lawful.","sourceNote":"Representative summary from master forms workflow.","aliases":["extension","variation","rural referral","non metro"],"searchTerms":["expired","destination","transport","rural","extension"],"riskLevel":"medium","indexedClock":"72 hours","indexedTerms":["referral","place","practitioner","examination","authorised","medical","time","date","72 hours"],"legalNote":"Confirm the referral assessment, destination/place and expiry before any downstream detention, transport or treatment step; referral is not itself treatment, detention, transport or force authority. Use only the current approved form or PSOLIS pathway where available; only appropriately authorised people should complete MHA 2014 forms. Authority is limited to the Act sections, signature block, time limits and wording on the approved form.","practicePearls":["Variation is only useful while the underlying pathway is still lawful.","Keep referral, detention, transport and treatment authorities separate in the record.","Clock cue: 72 hours. Record the start time, expiry or review point, and next owner.","Source cue: sections 45, 46."],"preUseChecks":["Before use: confirm the assessment basis, examination place, referral expiry and any linked detention or transport form.","Confirm the patient/person identifiers, maker, date, time, place and signature fields are complete.","Confirm copies, notices, support-person communication and filing/PSOLIS requirements before handover.","Open the official PDF when the form wording or authority boundary matters."],"actSections":[{"section":"45","title":"Extending referral made outside metropolitan area","summary":"Where a referral was made outside the metropolitan area and the person responsible for transporting the patient forms the view it will expire before arrival, an extension of a further 72 hours may be obtained. The request goes to the referring practitioner, or if they are unavailable another practitioner at the same place, or failing that any other MP or AMHP; the transporting person may extend it themselves only if no practitioner is reasonably available and they are themselves an MP or AMHP. The extension is recorded in the approved form with the time granted, the new expiry and the reasons, and filed with a copy to the person. A referral cannot be extended more than once.","reviewStatus":"drafted"},{"section":"46","title":"Changing place where examination will be conducted","summary":"An MP or AMHP may change the place specified in a s 26 referral where the examination will be conducted, but only after consulting a practitioner at the proposed new place. They must promptly tell whoever is transporting the person, record the change in the approved form with the old and new places and the time, and file it with a copy to the person. Changing between an authorised hospital and a non-hospital place switches which limb of s 26 the referral is treated as having been made under.","reviewStatus":"drafted"}],"sourceFacts":{"documentTitle":"Variation Of Referral","fileName":"📋 Form 1B.pdf","pages":2,"timings":["72 hours"],"sectionCue":"sections 45, 46","indexedAt":"Official form PDF indexed locally"},"availability":"downloadable","officialPdfUrl":"https://www.chiefpsychiatrist.wa.gov.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/FORM1B_MHA2014__public.pdf","officialRegisterUrl":"https://www.chiefpsychiatrist.wa.gov.au/laws-and-rights/legislation/mental-health-act-2014-forms/","localPdfPath":"/forms-pdf/form-1b.pdf","localPdfSha256":"e29fab5a3747d39c59201671c1e8165cdce9fca0006501946196fb3f3c3c88ed","localPdfBytes":199390,"officialPdfPasswordProtected":true,"officialTitleCheckedAt":"17 July 2026","archiveGeneratedAt":"2026-07-13T16:02:29.961824Z"}}},{"logicalId":"forms:form-2","logicalDocumentId":"ec718de6-ebc3-5062-a2fa-56893d14c096","logicalChunkId":"30259fca-6c2e-56a9-b345-6ac13c2d00f8","normalizedText":"Form: Order to detain voluntary inpatient in authorised hospital for assessment\nUse for a voluntary inpatient requesting discharge where urgent assessment is required.\nRoute: Parallel: 1A | After: Release, 1A, 3A\nEligibility: Assessment is required and no lawful next step has yet been completed.\nReferral: Before use: confirm live referral/order, detention place, expiry, receiving service and release/off-ramp trigger.\nLocation: Western Australia\nBest use: Detention authority must match the live referral or examination pathway, place, duration and expiry; do not use detention wording as treatment or transport authority. Use only the current approved form or PSOLIS pathway where available; only appropriately authorised people should complete MHA 2014 forms. Authority is limited to the Act sections, signature block, time limits and wording on the approved form.\nPrimary contact: Form 2 Official PDF\nTags: Form 2, Referral and detention, Mental Health Act 2014, voluntary inpatient, wants to leave, assessment hold, 6 hours, expired, hard stop, leave ward, discharge\nCatchments: Western Australia\norder to detain voluntary inpatient in authorised hospital for assessment form-2 use for a voluntary inpatient requesting discharge where urgent assessment is required. parallel 1a after release 1a 3a assessment is required and no lawful next step has yet been completed. official wa mental health act 2014 form before use confirm live referral/order detention place expiry receiving service and release/off-ramp trigger. western australia detention authority must match the live referral or examination pathway place duration and expiry do not use detention wording as treatment or transport authority. use only the current approved form or psolis pathway where available only appropriately authorised people should complete mha 2014 forms. authority is limited to the act sections signature block time limits and wording on the approved form. form 2 form 2 order to detain voluntary inpatient in authorised hospital for assessment referral and detention use for a voluntary inpatient requesting discharge where urgent assessment is required. 6 hours up to 6 hours inpatient voluntary treatment assessment authorised hospital time detained 6 hours up to 6 hours form 2 official pdf office of the chief psychiatrist wa approved mha 2014 forms source checked official register checked 17 july 2026 form 2 referral and detention mental health act 2014 voluntary inpatient wants to leave assessment hold 6 hours expired hard stop leave ward discharge western australia high risk referral and detention official pdf official public pdf https //www.chiefpsychiatrist.wa.gov.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/form2 mha2014 public.pdf current ocp source official forms register https //www.chiefpsychiatrist.wa.gov.au/laws-and-rights/legislation/mental-health-act-2014-forms/ check current availability clock / review maximum 6 hours. treat as a hard stop. 6 hours up to 6 hours made by / authority authorised clinician specified by the act pathway. short assessment hold for the voluntary inpatient pathway. criteria / threshold assessment is required and no lawful next step has yet been completed. ongoing detention beyond the maximum period or treatment without separate authority. act sections authority under the act 34 35 purpose use for a voluntary inpatient requesting discharge where urgent assessment is required. authorises short assessment hold for the voluntary inpatient pathway. does not authorise ongoing detention beyond the maximum period or treatment without separate authority. parallel 1a after release 1a 3a copies and filing hand over expiry and next owner clearly. documentation stem voluntary inpatient requested discharge at time . form 2 commenced because assessment reason . expiry and next lawful step documented. safety pearl the expiry is the clinical priority. decide and document the next lawful step early. common traps missing the 6-hour hard stop. static detention without active assessment. not documenting release/off-ramp. pre-use checks before use confirm live referral/order detention place expiry receiving service and release/off-ramp trigger. confirm the patient/person identifiers maker date time place and signature fields are complete. confirm copies notices support-person communication and filing/psolis requirements before handover. open the official pdf when the form wording or authority boundary matters. before use confirm live referral/order detention place expiry receiving service and release/off-ramp trigger. caution confirm the patient/person identifiers maker date time place and signature fields are complete. caution confirm copies notices support-person communication and filing/psolis requirements before handover. caution missing the 6-hour hard stop. reject static detention without active assessment. reject official title and availability checked 17 july 2026 archive guidance remains a prototype reference aid and requires local clinical/legal governance review use the current approved pdf or psolis form do not modify approved form content 2 referral and detention use for a voluntary inpatient requesting discharge where urgent assessment is required. authorised clinician specified by the act pathway. assessment is required and no lawful next step has yet been completed. maximum 6 hours. treat as a hard stop. short assessment hold for the voluntary inpatient pathway. ongoing detention beyond the maximum period or treatment without separate authority. voluntary inpatient wants to leave assessment hold 6 hours expired hard stop leave ward discharge inpatient voluntary treatment assessment authorised hospital time detained 6 hours up to 6 hours section 34 person in charge of ward may order assessment where a voluntary inpatient wants to leave against medical advice and the person in charge of the ward reasonably suspects on the section 25 criteria that they need an involuntary treatment order that person may order an assessment by an mp or amhp at the hospital. the inpatient can be detained for up to 6 hours to allow it. the order is in the approved form and is filed with a copy to the patient and the inpatient must be given the opportunity and means to contact a support person their treating health professional and the chief mental health advocate. detention ends at 6 hours if the assessment is not completed or is completed without a s 36 2 referral being made. section 35 revoking order for assessment the person who ordered a s 34 assessment may revoke that order at any time before the assessment starts if satisfied the patient no longer needs an involuntary treatment order. the revocation is in the approved form and is filed with a copy to the patient and detention cannot continue once it is made. form forms checklist assessment transfer template","contentHash":"cb5bf8c9be5fb981ef05ead9415c092f636418c9bb63ae799d4afe22a65af53d","publicationFingerprint":"6b841ec6ea4b918344306dd716b961fc908c1dccb535427e70caa860da971864","governanceFingerprint":"6473895da16d5508d03ffea998bc94f9de73dd719d70d551126b969e94bd3eab","lineageFingerprint":"4f53cda18c2baa0c0354bb5f9a3ecbe5ed12ab4d8e11ba873c2f11161202b945","publicMetadataFingerprint":"8d6495810ae19bbb4db7ba24a4d91dfa4a5ba4f5d365d497853d2a147cf4f3b0","record":{"version":"site-content-record-v1","logicalId":"forms:form-2","producerClass":"dynamic_registry","domain":"forms","route":"/forms/form-2","title":"Order to detain voluntary inpatient in authorised hospital for assessment","body":"Form: Order to detain voluntary inpatient in authorised hospital for assessment\nUse for a voluntary inpatient requesting discharge where urgent assessment is required.\nRoute: Parallel: 1A | After: Release, 1A, 3A\nEligibility: Assessment is required and no lawful next step has yet been completed.\nReferral: Before use: confirm live referral/order, detention place, expiry, receiving service and release/off-ramp trigger.\nLocation: Western Australia\nBest use: Detention authority must match the live referral or examination pathway, place, duration and expiry; do not use detention wording as treatment or transport authority. Use only the current approved form or PSOLIS pathway where available; only app