nuation Of Detention. Review the source snippets and approved form before use.","statusChips":[{"label":"high risk","tone":"danger"},{"label":"Referral and detention","tone":"info"},{"label":"Official PDF","tone":"success"}],"primaryContact":{"label":"Form code","value":"Form 3B","detail":"Official PDF","kind":"text"},"contacts":[{"label":"Official public PDF","value":"https://www.chiefpsychiatrist.wa.gov.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/FORM3B_MHA2014__public.pdf","detail":"Current OCP source","kind":"web"},{"label":"Official forms register","value":"https://www.chiefpsychiatrist.wa.gov.au/laws-and-rights/legislation/mental-health-act-2014-forms/","detail":"Check current availability","kind":"web"}],"route":"Confirm the current approved form pathway and local policy.","eligibility":"Use the threshold stated in the official form and any linked guidance.","cost":"Official WA Mental Health Act 2014 form","referral":"Before use: confirm live referral/order, detention place, expiry, receiving service and release/off-ramp trigger.","location":"Western Australia","summaryCards":[{"id":"clock","label":"Clock / review","title":"24 hours, 72 hours, 144 hours, 48 hours, up to 24 hours"},{"id":"authority","label":"Made by / authority","title":"Check the official form signature block and Act sections.","detail":"Authority is limited to what the approved form and Act section state."},{"id":"criteria","label":"Criteria / threshold","title":"Use the threshold stated in the official form and any linked guidance.","detail":"Does not replace linked forms, consent, notification or reporting duties unless the source says so."},{"id":"act-sections","label":"Act sections","title":"Authority under the Act","detail":"28 · 59 · 62"}],"referralInfo":[{"label":"Purpose","value":"Official form source: Continuation Of Detention. Review the source snippets and approved form before use."},{"label":"Authorises","value":"Authority is limited to what the approved form and Act section state."},{"label":"Does not authorise","value":"Does not replace linked forms, consent, notification or reporting duties unless the source says so."},{"label":"Copies and filing","value":"Follow the approved distribution and filing fields on the form."},{"label":"Documentation stem","value":"Source-backed note for Form 3B: document maker, section, threshold facts, clock, destination/place, notifications and next owner."},{"label":"Safety pearl","value":"Open the source snippets before relying on the pathway."},{"label":"Common traps","value":"Do not infer powers beyond the form wording. Check linked forms, attachments, notifications and clock limits."},{"label":"Pre-use checks","value":"Before use: confirm live referral/order, detention place, expiry, receiving service and release/off-ramp trigger. Confirm the patient/person identifiers, maker, date, time, place and signature fields are complete. Confirm copies, notices, support-person communication and filing/PSOLIS requirements before handover. Open the official PDF when the form wording or authority boundary matters."}],"bestUse":"Detention authority must match the live referral or examination pathway, place, duration and expiry; do not use detention wording as treatment or transport authority. Use only the current approved form or PSOLIS pathway where available; only appropriately authorised people should complete MHA 2014 forms. Authority is limited to the Act sections, signature block, time limits and wording on the approved form.","criteria":[{"label":"Before use: confirm live referral/order, detention place, expiry, receiving service and release/off-ramp trigger.","tone":"caution"},{"label":"Confirm the patient/person identifiers, maker, date, time, place and signature fields are complete.","tone":"caution"},{"label":"Confirm copies, notices, support-person communication and filing/PSOLIS requirements before handover.","tone":"caution"},{"label":"Do not infer powers beyond the form wording.","tone":"reject"},{"label":"Check linked forms, attachments, notifications and clock limits.","tone":"reject"}],"verification":{"locallyVerified":false,"confidence":"Medium","notes":["Official title and availability checked 17 July 2026","Archive guidance remains a prototype reference aid and requires local clinical/legal governance review","Use the current approved PDF or PSOLIS form; do not modify approved form content"]},"tags":["Form 3B","Referral and detention","Mental Health Act 2014","3b","continuation of detention","detention","hospital","place","hours","authorised","psychiatrist","practitioner","continuation","24 hours","72 hours","144 hours","48 hours","up to 24 hours"],"catchments":["Western Australia"],"catalogueLabel":"Form 3B","navigatorQuery":"Form 3B Continuation of detention Referral and detention Official form source: Continuation Of Detention. Review the source snippets and approved form before use.","source":{"label":"Office of the Chief Psychiatrist WA — approved MHA 2014 forms","status":"Source checked","url":"https://www.chiefpsychiatrist.wa.gov.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/FORM3B_MHA2014__public.pdf","reviewed":"Official register checked 17 July 2026","notes":["Open the official source to confirm the current approved version before use","PSOLIS is the preferred completion method where available"]},"catalogPayload":{"id":"form-3b","form":"3B","name":"Continuation of detention","category":"Referral and detention","purpose":"Official form source: Continuation Of Detention. Review the source snippets and approved form before use.","maker":"Check the official form signature block and Act sections.","involved":"Confirm patient, maker, receiving service, support contacts and required notifications from the form.","threshold":"Use the threshold stated in the official form and any linked guidance.","clock":"24 hours, 72 hours, 144 hours, 48 hours, up to 24 hours","destination":"Confirm destination/place fields on the approved form.","authorises":"Authority is limited to what the approved form and Act section state.","doesNotAuthorise":"Does not replace linked forms, consent, notification or reporting duties unless the source says so.","before":[],"parallel":[],"after":[],"copies":"Follow the approved distribution and filing fields on the form.","documentationStem":"Source-backed note for Form 3B: document maker, section, threshold facts, clock, destination/place, notifications and next owner.","traps":["Do not infer powers beyond the form wording.","Check linked forms, attachments, notifications and clock limits."],"safetyPearl":"Open the source snippets before relying on the pathway.","sourceNote":"Indexed from 📋 Form 3B.pdf.","aliases":["3b","continuation of detention","detention"],"searchTerms":["detention","hospital","place","hours","authorised","psychiatrist","practitioner","continuation","24 hours","72 hours","144 hours","48 hours","up to 24 hours"],"riskLevel":"high","indexedTerms":[],"legalNote":"Detention authority must match the live referral or examination pathway, place, duration and expiry; do not use detention wording as treatment or transport authority. Use only the current approved form or PSOLIS pathway where available; only appropriately authorised people should complete MHA 2014 forms. Authority is limited to the Act sections, signature block, time limits and wording on the approved form.","practicePearls":["Open the source snippets before relying on the pathway.","The lawful clock and destination are the safety-critical parts of detention forms.","Clock cue: 24 hours, 72 hours, 144 hours. Record the start time, expiry or review point, and next owner.","Source cue: sections 28, 59, 62."],"preUseChecks":["Before use: confirm live referral/order, detention place, expiry, receiving service and release/off-ramp trigger.","Confirm the patient/person identifiers, maker, date, time, place and signature fields are complete.","Confirm copies, notices, support-person communication and filing/PSOLIS requirements before handover.","Open the official PDF when the form wording or authority boundary matters."],"actSections":[{"section":"28","title":"Detention to enable person to be taken to authorised hospital or other place","summary":"An MP or AMHP may order detention for up to 24 hours to enable a referred person to be taken to the examination place, and may renew it for further 24-hour blocks — but only after personally assessing the person again and remaining satisfied detention is still needed. Total continuous detention is capped at 72 hours if the referral was made in the metropolitan area, or 144 hours outside it. The order is in the approved form with times made and expiring, reasons and the practitioner's details, is filed with a copy to the person, and is a Part 9 notifiable event. The person must be given the opportunity and means to contact a support person, their treating health professional and the Chief Mental Health Advocate. Detention ends if the person has not been taken to the place and no valid further order or transport-order apprehension applies, or if the referral expires first.","reviewStatus":"drafted"},{"section":"59","title":"Detention at place outside metropolitan area","summary":"Where the examination place is outside the metropolitan area and it is not practicable to finish the examination within the 24 hours allowed by s 58(1)(b), an MP or AMHP at that place may order detention to continue for up to a further 48 hours so it can be completed. The order is in the approved form with the times made and expiring, the reasons and the practitioner's details, and is filed with a copy to the person. The person must be given the opportunity and means to contact a support person, their treating health professional and the Chief Mental Health Advocate. Detention ends at the 48 hours if the examination is unfinished, or is finished without a s 61(1) order.","reviewStatus":"drafted"},{"section":"62","title":"Detention to enable person to be taken to hospital","summary":"An MP or AMHP may order detention to continue for up to 24 hours so a person under a s 61(1)(a) or (c) order can be taken to the hospital, and may renew it in further 24-hour blocks — but only after assessing the person immediately beforehand and remaining satisfied detention is still needed. Total continuous detention under this section cannot exceed 72 hours. The order is in the approved form with the times made and expiring, the reasons and the practitioner's details, is filed with a copy to the person, and the person must be given the opportunity and means to contact a support person, their treating health professional and the Chief Mental Health Advocate. Detention ends if the person has not reached the hospital, has not been apprehended under a s 63 transport order, and no valid further order applies.","reviewStatus":"drafted"}],"sourceFacts":{"documentTitle":"Continuation Of Detention","fileName":"📋 Form 3B.pdf","pages":2,"timings":["24 hours","72 hours","144 hours","48 hours","up to 24 hours"],"sectionCue":"sections 28, 59, 62","indexedAt":"Official form PDF indexed locally"},"availability":"downloadable","officialPdfUrl":"https://www.chiefpsychiatrist.wa.gov.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/FORM3B_MHA2014__public.pdf","officialRegisterUrl":"https://www.chiefpsychiatrist.wa.gov.au/laws-and-rights/legislation/mental-health-act-2014-forms/","localPdfPath":"/forms-pdf/form-3b.pdf","localPdfSha256":"3bf44962f5570a588f80ae57f3afced7b3c9dd8cc61f8d2ec86a7943c98d7850","localPdfBytes":198242,"officialPdfPasswordProtected":true,"officialTitleCheckedAt":"17 July 2026","archiveGeneratedAt":"2026-07-13T16:02:29.961824Z"}}},{"logicalId":"forms:form-3c","logicalDocumentId":"bbdbaa9b-dadb-5e8f-8296-68ebace9e244","logicalChunkId":"ee37a685-21c3-5a1b-a6dd-872dda271e7c","normalizedText":"Form: Continuation of detention to enable a further examination by a psychiatrist\nOfficial form source: Continuation Of Detention To Enable A Further Examination By A Psychiatrist. Review the source snippets