ransfer order","category":"Transport and transfer","purpose":"The official register lists this form, but it is currently unavailable. Check the register and local governance before proceeding.","maker":"Only an appropriately authorised person under the Mental Health Act 2014 and the approved form instructions.","involved":"Confirm the required recipients, support persons, records and local PSOLIS workflow on the current approved form.","threshold":"Confirm the statutory criteria and completion instructions on the current approved form before use.","clock":"Confirm any time limit, expiry or review point on the current approved form and local policy.","destination":"Confirm any required place or destination on the approved form.","authorises":"Only the action or record expressly described by Form 4E and the Mental Health Act 2014.","doesNotAuthorise":"No action beyond the current Act, approved form wording and the maker’s lawful authority.","before":[],"parallel":[],"after":[],"copies":"Confirm notices, copies, handover and filing requirements on the approved form.","documentationStem":"","traps":[],"safetyPearl":"Open the current official source and confirm authority, timing, notices and filing requirements before completion.","sourceNote":"Official title and availability checked against the Office of the Chief Psychiatrist register.","aliases":[],"searchTerms":[],"riskLevel":"medium","indexedTerms":[],"legalNote":"Use only the current approved form or PSOLIS pathway. This catalogue is a reference aid, not legal advice, and does not replace the Act, form instructions or local governance.","practicePearls":["Treat the approved form and current legislation as authoritative."],"preUseChecks":["Open the current official form or PSOLIS workflow before use.","Confirm the maker is appropriately authorised and all statutory criteria are met.","Confirm identifiers, date, time, signatures, notices, copies and filing requirements."],"actSections":[{"section":"557","title":"Transfer from interstate mental health service to hospital","summary":"The person in charge of a hospital may, with the Chief Psychiatrist's written consent, make a transfer approval order approving an interstate inpatient's transfer to that hospital — including one absent without leave as described in s 551(3). The order is in the approved form and must include the patient's name, the interstate service transferred from and the hospital transferred to, the time made, the reasons and the maker's details. A copy of both the consent and the order must be transmitted to the interstate service as soon as practicable. On admission the interstate inpatient treatment order is taken to be an inpatient treatment order made under this Act, and the consent and order must then be filed with a copy of each given to the patient. Making it is a Part 9 notifiable event.","reviewStatus":"drafted"}],"availability":"unavailable","officialRegisterUrl":"https://www.chiefpsychiatrist.wa.gov.au/laws-and-rights/legislation/mental-health-act-2014-forms/","officialTitleCheckedAt":"17 July 2026","archiveGeneratedAt":"2026-07-13T16:02:29.961824Z"}}},{"logicalId":"forms:form-5a","logicalDocumentId":"ad38e16f-5168-553b-a64d-d972a1e54a18","logicalChunkId":"82178045-5c55-55b6-8ece-53a479533c06","normalizedText":"Form: Community Treatment Order\nUse where compulsory treatment can be safely managed in the community.\nRoute: Before: 1A | Parallel: 5F | After: Continuation, variation, revocation\nEligibility: Treatment order criteria met and community treatment is the least restrictive suitable pathway.\nReferral: Before use: confirm criteria, capacity/consent reasoning where relevant, authorised setting, review date and notifications.\nLocation: Western Australia\nBest use: Treatment order forms should show criteria, least restrictive reasoning, authorised setting, review timing and required notices. Use only the current approved form or PSOLIS pathway where available; only appropriately authorised people should complete MHA 2014 forms. Authority is limited to the Act sections, signature block, time limits and wording on the approved form.\nPrimary contact: Form 5A Official PDF\nTags: Form 5A, Community treatment orders, Mental Health Act 2014, CTO, community treatment, 5a order, least restrictive, community, breach, conditions\nCatchments: Western Australia\ncommunity treatment order form-5a use where compulsory treatment can be safely managed in the community. before 1a parallel 5f after continuation variation revocation treatment order criteria met and community treatment is the least restrictive suitable pathway. official wa mental health act 2014 form before use confirm criteria capacity/consent reasoning where relevant authorised setting review date and notifications. western australia treatment order forms should show criteria least restrictive reasoning authorised setting review timing and required notices. use only the current approved form or psolis pathway where available only appropriately authorised people should complete mha 2014 forms. authority is limited to the act sections signature block time limits and wording on the approved form. form 5a form 5a community treatment order community treatment orders use where compulsory treatment can be safely managed in the community. up to 3 months within 72 hours not more than 3 months within 14 days 7 days within 7 days treatment community psychiatrist patient time practitioner made making up to 3 months within 72 hours not more than 3 months within 14 days 7 days within 7 days form 5a official pdf office of the chief psychiatrist wa approved mha 2014 forms source checked official register checked 17 july 2026 form 5a community treatment orders mental health act 2014 cto community treatment 5a order least restrictive community breach conditions western australia medium risk community treatment orders official pdf official public pdf https //www.chiefpsychiatrist.wa.gov.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/form5a mha2014 public.pdf current ocp source official forms register https //www.chiefpsychiatrist.wa.gov.au/laws-and-rights/legislation/mental-health-act-2014-forms/ check current availability clock / review review and continuation dates must be diarised. up to 3 months within 72 hours not more than 3 months within 14 days 7 days within 7 days made by / authority psychiatrist or authorised pathway decision-maker. compulsory treatment in the community according to cto conditions. criteria / threshold treatment order criteria met and community treatment is the least restrictive suitable pathway. inpatient detention unless a separate pathway applies. act sections authority under the act 11 sections cited purpose use where compulsory treatment can be safely managed in the community. authorises compulsory treatment in the community according to cto conditions. does not authorise inpatient detention unless a separate pathway applies. before 1a parallel 5f after continuation variation revocation copies and filing provide order details and conditions to relevant parties according to local process. documentation stem cto considered least restrictive because community supports/risks . conditions and responsible service documented. safety pearl least restrictive reasoning should be visible not implied. common traps using inpatient logic without community feasibility analysis. conditions not communicated. pre-use checks before use confirm criteria capacity/consent reasoning where relevant authorised setting review date and notifications. confirm the patient/person identifiers maker date time place and signature fields are complete. confirm copies notices support-person communication and filing/psolis requirements before handover. open the official pdf when the form wording or authority boundary matters. before use confirm criteria capacity/consent reasoning where relevant authorised setting review date and notifications. caution confirm the patient/person identifiers maker date time place and signature fields are complete. caution confirm copies notices support-person communication and filing/psolis requirements before handover. caution using inpatient logic without community feasibility analysis. reject conditions not communicated. reject official title and availability checked 17 july 2026 archive guidance remains a prototype reference aid and requires local clinical/legal governance review use the current approved pdf or psolis form do not modify approved form content 5a community treatment orders use where compulsory treatment can be safely managed in the community. psychiatrist or authorised pathway decision-maker. treatment order criteria met and community treatment is the least restrictive suitable pathway. review and continuation dates must be diarised. compulsory treatment in the community according to cto conditions. inpatient detention unless a separate pathway applies. cto community treatment 5a order least restrictive community breach conditions treatment community psychiatrist patient time practitioner made making up to 3 months within 72 hours not more than 3 months within 14 days 7 days within 7 days section 55 what psychiatrist must do on completing examination on completing the examination the psychiatrist must make one of four orders an inpatient treatment order detaining the person at the authorised hospital for a s 87 period a community treatment order an order continuing detention to allow a further psychiatrist examination or an order that the person cannot continue to be detained. the order is in the approved form with the time the reasons except for a release order and the psychiatrist s details and is filed with a copy to the person. a continuation order runs only to the period specified which cannot exceed 72 hours from reception or detention at the hospital and cannot be extended. making the order is a part 9 notifiable event. section 56 effect of order for continuation of detention an order continuing detention under 