g psychiatrist/service review date notices and breach response pathway. caution confirm the patient/person identifiers maker date time place and signature fields are complete. caution confirm copies notices support-person communication and filing/psolis requirements before handover. caution do not infer powers beyond the form wording. reject check linked forms attachments notifications and clock limits. reject official title and availability checked 17 july 2026 archive guidance remains a prototype reference aid and requires local clinical/legal governance review use the current approved pdf or psolis form do not modify approved form content 5d community treatment orders official form source request for practitioner to conduct monthly examination of a patient. review the source snippets and approved form before use. check the official form signature block and act sections. use the threshold stated in the official form and any linked guidance. within 14 days 2 months authority is limited to what the approved form and act section state. does not replace linked forms consent notification or reporting duties unless the source says so. 5d request for practitioner to conduct monthly examination of a patient community treatment order examination psychiatrist supervising practitioner patient request monthly conduct within 14 days 2 months section 118 monthly examination of patient an involuntary community patient must be examined on or within 14 days before the day each monthly review period ends by the supervising psychiatrist or by another medical practitioner or mental health practitioner if the supervising psychiatrist is unavailable or has requested it under s 119 1 . another practitioner cannot conduct that examination if more than 2 months have passed since the supervising psychiatrist last examined the patient. a practitioner examining in the supervising psychiatrist s place must provide a written report recommending whether on the section 25 criteria the patient st