s":[{"section":"128","title":"Order to attend if non-compliance continues","summary":"Where the patient has been given a breach notice and the supervising psychiatrist is not satisfied they are complying, the psychiatrist may make an order to attend requiring the patient to attend a specified time and place to be provided with treatment. The order must warn that non-compliance may result in a transport order authorising apprehension and transport to that place. It is in the approved form with the time made, the reasons, the time and place to attend, the warning and the psychiatrist's details, and is filed with a copy to the patient.","reviewStatus":"drafted"}],"sourceFacts":{"documentTitle":"Order To Attend","fileName":"📋 Form 5F.pdf","pages":2,"timings":["Check timing","expiry and review requirements in the source."],"sectionCue":"sections 128","indexedAt":"Official form PDF indexed locally"},"availability":"downloadable","officialPdfUrl":"https://www.chiefpsychiatrist.wa.gov.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/FORM5F_MHA2014__public.pdf","officialRegisterUrl":"https://www.chiefpsychiatrist.wa.gov.au/laws-and-rights/legislation/mental-health-act-2014-forms/","localPdfPath":"/forms-pdf/form-5f.pdf","localPdfSha256":"e6acb4384559988ec06063dc6f7b6873d8f3d95df811c12c153c409ceae061e0","localPdfBytes":300775,"officialPdfPasswordProtected":true,"officialTitleCheckedAt":"17 July 2026","archiveGeneratedAt":"2026-07-13T16:02:29.961824Z"}}},{"logicalId":"forms:form-6a","logicalDocumentId":"7a86a042-a470-554d-bff0-f8afdea56264","logicalChunkId":"20c238c1-3ba7-5bfc-ab02-726bb2db20d9","normalizedText":"Form: Inpatient treatment order in authorised hospital\nUse where inpatient compulsory treatment in an authorised hospital is required.\nRoute: Before: 1A | Parallel: 7A | After: Continuation, leave, revocation, CTO\nEligibility: Inpatient treatment order criteria met and less restrictive options are insufficient.\nReferral: Before use: confirm criteria, capacity/consent reasoning where relevant, authorised setting, review date and notifications.\nLocation: Western Australia\nBest use: Treatment order forms should show criteria, least restrictive reasoning, authorised setting, review timing and required notices. Use only the current approved form or PSOLIS pathway where available; only appropriately authorised people should complete MHA 2014 forms. Authority is limited to the Act sections, signature block, time limits and wording on the approved form.\nPrimary contact: Form 6A Official PDF\nTags: Form 6A, Inpatient treatment orders, Mental Health Act 2014, inpatient order, authorised hospital, 6a, least restrictive, review, inpatient\nCatchments: Western Australia\ninpatient treatment order in authorised hospital form-6a use where inpatient compulsory treatment in an authorised hospital is required. before 1a parallel 7a after continuation leave revocation cto inpatient treatment order criteria met and less restrictive options are insufficient. official wa mental health act 2014 form before use confirm criteria capacity/consent reasoning where relevant authorised setting review date and notifications. western australia treatment order forms should show criteria least restrictive reasoning authorised setting review timing and required notices. use only the current approved form or psolis pathway where available only appropriately authorised people should complete mha 2014 forms. authority is limited to the act sections signature block time limits and wording on the approved form. form 6a form 6a inpatient treatment order in authorised hospital inpatient treatment orders use where inpatient compulsory treatment in an authorised hospital is required. up to 21 days 14 days 21 days within 7 days treatment inpatient psychiatrist making involuntary time patient authorised up to 21 days 14 days 21 days within 7 days form 6a official pdf office of the chief psychiatrist wa approved mha 2014 forms source checked official register checked 17 july 2026 form 6