 migraine prophylaxis, IBS-D, severe insomnia. Clinical Place First-line low-dose adjunct for chronic nerve pain (e.g., post-herpetic neuralgia, diabetic neuropathy). Contraindications & Populations contra Absolute CRITICAL — Recent myocardial infarction, heart block, severe hepatic impairment, concurrent MAOIs. Elderly CRITICAL — Heavily featured on the Beers Criteria. Causes falls, confusion, and urinary retention. Use Nortriptyline instead if a TCA is required. Pregnancy CAUTION — **Pregnancy** Category C. Key Interactions inter Pharmacodynamic CRITICAL — MAOIs, Tramadol (Serotonin Syndrome). Pharmacodynamic HIGH — Additive anticholinergic burden (Oxybutynin, Promethazine). Pharmacokinetic HIGH — **CYP2D6** inhibitors (Fluoxetine, Paroxetine) spike TCA blood levels into the toxic range. Monitoring & Cautions mon Cardiac MANDATORY — Baseline **ECG** (Check QTc and QRS width) before escalating doses. Bedside Monitor for urinary retention and severe constipation. Clinical Pearls pearl The Overdose Antidote If a patient overdoses on Amitriptyline, their QRS will widen on the ECG. You MUST push IV Sodium Bicarbonate. It overwhelms the sodium channel blockade and saves the heart. Take Early To avoid the brutal 'morning hangover', tell patients to take their dose at 7 PM or 8 PM, not right before bed at 11 PM. Mechanism & Pharmacokinetics evid Mechanism Inhibits reuptake of Serotonin and Noradrenaline. Also heavily blocks Histamine (H1), Muscarinic (M1), and Alpha-1 adrenergic receptors, driving its massive side effect profile. Onset Sedation is immediate. Pain relief takes 2-4 weeks. Half-life 10-28 hours. Metabolised by CYP2D6/CYP2C19 to active nortriptyline. Sources src Source Review Source Check - ENDEP Australian PI/CMI, ARTG 71044/59788/64425, and PBS search checked 2026-05-10 for antidepressant batch appraisal: identity/access, indication, dosing, contraindications/populations, interactions, monitoring, patient-context metadata, and source-row status.\nClass & Ro