ase II (so bradykinin does not accumulate). Onset **PO** 2-3 hours. Half-life 9 hours (Prodrug converted to active candesartan in the gut wall). Sources src Source Review Source-backed review 2026-05-11: ATACAND/candesartan Australian ARTG-CMI source pack. Entry checked for dosing, access, contraindications/populations, interactions, monitoring, patient-context metadata, and app structure.\nClass & Role ARB — Angiotensin II Receptor Blocker (ARB). Route / Formulation Tablets (4, 8, 16, 32 mg). (Atacand) Usual Dose & Max Start **PO** 8-16 mg **OD**. Max 32 mg/day. Key Indication Doses Hypertension: Start **PO** 8-16 mg **OD**. Max 32 mg/day. Heart Failure (HFrEF): Start **PO** 4 mg **OD**. Titrate doubling the dose every 2 weeks to target 32 mg **OD**. Renal Impairment: Start at 4 mg **OD** if **eGFR** < 30. Monitor K+. Best Uses Candesartan is the ideal ACE inhibitor substitute (no cough) with unique migraine prophylaxis evidence, but carries identical renal and pregnancy risks to ACEis. Avoid / Cautions Bilateral renal artery stenosis, severe hepatic impairment/cholestasis. **Pregnancy** Category D. Causes fetal renal failure/death. Key Risks Renal: Hyperkalemia, AKI in volume-depleted patients. Cardiovascular: Orthostatic hypotension, dizziness. Respiratory: Incidence of dry cough is equivalent to placebo. Key Interactions ARB + Diuretic + NSAID (Guaranteed AKI). Additive hyperkalemia with Spironolactone or Trimethoprim. Monitoring Check **U&E** 1-2 weeks post-initiation. Check **BP**. Clinical Pearl Candesartan has strong, unique evidence for Migraine Prophylaxis (off-label). It is frequently prescribed by neurologists to prevent chronic migraines while simultaneously treating the patient's blood pressure.","sourceRole":"clinical_reference","access":"public","validationStatus":"unverified","sourceStatus":"current","sourceLineage":[],"publicationVersion":"60367667d84c9d27a6fcce76997c60804d6c95b1544ca8195f35dc17305b93f9","contentHash":"0c0f2a5edda3ecce10efa36a4b926