astrointestinal: Severe dry mouth, constipation, urinary retention. Key Interactions MAOIs, Tramadol (Serotonin Syndrome). Additive CNS depression with alcohol. CYP2D6 inhibitors (Fluoxetine, Paroxetine) spike levels into the lethal range. Monitoring Baseline and routine **ECG** (monitoring QTc and QRS width) is absolutely essential. Actively attempt to cross-taper the patient to an SSRI or Nortriptyline if they are admitted to the ward. Clinical Pearl Of all the TCAs (which are already dangerous), Dosulepin has the highest toxicity index. The gap between a dose that fixes depression and a dose that stops the heart is frighteningly small.","sourceRole":"clinical_reference","access":"public","validationStatus":"unverified","sourceStatus":"current","sourceLineage":[],"publicationVersion":"a064416b0b0145f9006caa4ba1bc705681c038ed9db47d4be217fea73155fb92","contentHash":"9c63d837b2472fb82051c20f092cef26c98eee15ce4afe2cefe374b5c1a5d3c4"},"renderPayload":{"slug":"dosulepin","name":"Dosulepin","class":"Antidepressant","subclass":"TCA","category":"Psychiatry - Antidepressants","accent":"#7c3aed","tag":"TCA","schedule":"S4","stats":[{"label":"Max Dose","value":"225 mg/day","cls":"hi","flag":"hi"},{"label":"Half-life","value":"11-24 h","cls":"","flag":""},{"label":"Toxicity in OD","value":"FATAL","cls":"hi","flag":"warn"},{"label":"Anticholinergic","value":"HIGH","cls":"warn","flag":""}],"sections":[{"title":"Rapid Summary","type":"summary","rows":[{"key":"Overview","val":"Tricyclic Antidepressant (also known as Dothiepin). Historically popular but now considered the most dangerous TCA in overdose due to profound cardiac toxicity.","tags":[]},{"key":"Maximum Dose","val":"Max **225 mg/day** (Usually 75-150 mg NOCTE).","tags":[]},{"key":"Clinical Focus","val":"Do not initiate. TGA guidelines actively discourage prescribing Dosulepin due to the unacceptably narrow margin between therapeutic dose and fatal overdose.","tags":[]},{"key":"Bottom Line","val":"Dosulepin is a TCA with n