lar events. Clinical Place Direct competitor to Semaglutide. Highly effective for T2DM with established cardiovascular disease. Contraindications & Populations contra Absolute CRITICAL — Personal/family history of Medullary Thyroid Carcinoma or MEN 2. History of pancreatitis. Surgery MANDATORY — Withhold prior to general anaesthesia due to delayed gastric emptying/aspiration risk. Pregnancy ABSOLUTE — **Pregnancy** Category D. Key Interactions inter Pharmacokinetic MODERATE — Delayed gastric emptying can slightly delay the absorption of concomitant oral medications. Monitoring & Cautions mon Bedside Counsel the patient to place the pen flat against the skin, unlock it, and press the button. They will hear a click, wait 5-10 seconds, hear a second click, and it is done. They never see the needle. Laboratory Routine **HbA1c**, **U&E**, and **Weight**. Clinical Pearls pearl The Compliance King Because the needle is 100% invisible and the dose is pre-measured (no dial to turn like Ozempic), Dulaglutide has the highest patient compliance rate among the injectable diabetes drugs, particularly in the elderly or needle-phobic. The 'Full' Feeling Educate the patient to stop eating the moment they feel full. Pushing past the 'full' signal while on a GLP-1 will guarantee severe vomiting. Mechanism & Pharmacokinetics evid Mechanism GLP-1 analogue fused to an IgG4 Fc fragment. This massive molecular size prevents it from being filtered by the kidneys and shields it from DPP-4 degradation. Onset Days. Half-life 5 Days (Allows once-weekly dosing). Sources src Source Review Source Check - TRULICITY ARTG/PI, PBS search, and TGA GLP-1 aspiration warning checked 2026-05-13 for high-risk opioid/general batch appraisal: identity/access, indication, dosing, contraindications/populations, interactions, monitoring, pregnancy/lactation, patient-context metadata, and source-row status.\nClass & Role GLP-1 Agonist — Once-weekly GLP-1 receptor agonist. Route / Formulation Single-use, pre-fille