 CRITICAL — Avoid concurrent QTc prolonging drugs. Pharmacokinetic HIGH — **CYP2D6** inhibitors (Paroxetine) spike Flupentixol levels. Monitoring & Cautions mon Bedside MANDATORY — Monitor for akathisia (pacing/restlessness). If the patient complains of severe anxiety post-injection, it is likely akathisia. Treat with Propranolol. Cardiac Baseline **ECG** (QTc check). Clinical Pearls pearl The Depot Pair Flupentixol and Zuclopenthixol are sister drugs. Remember: Flupentixol = Fly (Activating/Energy). Zuclopenthixol = Zzz (Sleeping/Sedating). Choose the depot based on whether the patient is withdrawn or aggressive. The Z-Track Necessity Must be injected deep IM using the Z-Track method to trap the oil in the muscle and prevent painful sterile subcutaneous abscesses. Mechanism & Pharmacokinetics evid Mechanism Thioxanthene derivative. Esterified with decanoic acid. At low doses, it blocks presynaptic D2 autoreceptors (boosting dopamine release, causing activation). At higher doses, it blocks postsynaptic D2 receptors (antipsychotic effect). Onset Days. Steady state takes 3 months. Half-life 17 Days (Released slowly from the oil depot). Sources src Source Review Source Check - FLUANXOL DEPOT ARTG/PI and PBS search checked 2026-05-10 for antipsychotic/LAI batch appraisal: identity/access, indication, dosing, contraindications/populations, interactions, monitoring, patient-context metadata, and source-row status.\nClass & Role FGA Depot — First-Generation Antipsychotic (FGA) depot. Route / Formulation Ampoules (20 mg/1 mL). Thin oil suspension. (Fluanxol Depot) Usual Dose & Max **IM** 20-40 mg every 2 to 4 weeks. Deep gluteal injection (Z-Track method). Max **40 mg/week** (Usually dosed 20-40 mg every 2-4 weeks). Key Indication Doses Schizophrenia Maintenance: **IM** 20-40 mg every 2 to 4 weeks. Deep gluteal injection (Z-Track method). Elderly / Frail: Start with 10-20 mg every 4 weeks. Highly sensitive to EPS. Best Uses Flupentixol decanoate is a depot thioxanthene antipsychotic for maintenance treatment of schizophrenia, but causes extrapyramidal effects and depression can emerge, and effects persist for weeks after injection. Avoid / Cautions Severely agitated or hyperactive patients, Parkinson's disease, severe CNS depression. **Pregnancy** Category C. Key Risks Neurological: Severe Extrapyramidal Side Effects (Parkinsonism, acute dystonia, severe akathisia). HIGH — Insomnia, agitation, over-stimulation. Cardiovascular: **QTc** prolongation, mild tachycardia. Endocrine: Hyperprolactinemia. Key Interactions Avoid concurrent QTc prolonging drugs. **CYP2D6** inhibitors (Paroxetine) spike Flupentixol levels. Monitoring Monitor for akathisia (pacing/restlessness). If the patient complains of severe anxiety post-injection, it is likely akathisia. Treat with Propranolol. Baseline **ECG** (QTc check). Clinical Pearl Flupentixol and Zuclopenthixol are sister drugs. Remember: Flupentixol = Fly (Activating/Energy). Zuclopenthixol = Zzz (Sleeping/Sedating). Choose the depot based on whether the patient is withdrawn or aggressive.","sourceRole":"clinical_reference","access":"public","validationStatus":"unverified","sourceStatus":"current","sourceLineage":[],"publicationVersion":"41c3a418039cbf9a2908b520f01e43ee1fc77ef4a1a34bca1499f32557961b9a","contentHash":"d76c7880b3092fce5641f8a170b5c7a98220b3eece361147393706c81aedc7d5"},"renderPayload":{"slug":"flupentixol-decanoate","name":"Flupentixol decanoate","class":"LAI Antipsychotic","subclass":"FGA Depot","category":"Psychiatry - Depot Antipsychotics","accent":"#0d9488","tag":"DEPOT Q2-4W","schedule":"S4","stats":[{"label":"Max Dose","value":"40 mg/week","cls":"hi","flag":"hi"},{"label":"Half-life","value":"17 Days","cls":"","flag":""},{"label":"Activation","value":"HIGH","cls":"warn","flag":""},{"label":"EPS Risk","value":"CRITICAL","cls":"hi","flag":"warn"}],"sections":[{"title":"Rapid Summary","type":"summary","rows":[{"key":"Overview","val":"First-Generation Antipsychotic (FGA) depot. Extre