ory A; routine preconception/early-pregnancy supplementation, with high-dose folate for higher-risk patients. Key Interactions inter Pharmacodynamic CRITICAL — Methotrexate. Folate replaces the exact compound Methotrexate is trying to starve the body of. If taken on the *same day*, the Folate will cancel out the Methotrexate, causing a severe arthritis flare. Must be staggered. Pharmacokinetic HIGH — Phenytoin and Barbiturates lower folate levels, and paradoxically, giving folate can lower Phenytoin levels, risking seizures. Monitoring & Cautions mon Laboratory MANDATORY — Always check both Serum Folate AND Vitamin B12 levels together before initiating treatment. Monitor **FBC**. Clinical Pearls pearl The Anticonvulsant Risk Women taking Valproate or Carbamazepine for epilepsy are at a massively increased risk of having a baby with spina bifida (due to folate depletion). They MUST be on the high-dose 5 mg folic acid tablet, not the standard 0.5 mg pregnancy multivitamin. Mechanism & Pharmacokinetics evid Mechanism Converted in the body to tetrahydrofolate. Acts as a methyl donor for the synthesis of purines and pyrimidines (DNA/RNA). Essential for normal erythropoiesis. Onset Days (Reticulocyte count peaks in 5-7 days). Half-life Hours (Water soluble, excess is rapidly excreted in urine). Sources src Source Review Source-backed review 2026-05-12: NHMRC/Eat For Health folate nutrient reference source pack. Entry checked for dosing, access, contraindications/populations, interactions, monitoring, patient-context metadata, and app structure.\nClass & Role Water-Soluble (B9) — Vitamin B9. Route / Formulation Tablets (0.5 mg, 5 mg). (Megafol) Usual Dose & Max **PO** 5 mg **OD** for 4 months. Max **5 mg/day**. Key Indication Doses Megaloblastic Anemia: **PO** 5 mg **OD** for 4 months. Pregnancy Prophylaxis: **PO** 0.5 mg **OD** (Start 1 month before conception). Give 5 mg OD if high risk (e.g., on Valproate/Carbamazepine). Methotrexate Rescue: **PO** 5 mg ONCE WEEKLY. Must be taken 1 to 2 days *after* the Methotrexate dose. Best Uses Folic acid is critical for neural tube defect prevention in pregnancy and managing folate deficiency, but must never be given alone if B12 deficiency is not excluded as it can mask and worsen neurological damage. Avoid / Cautions Undiagnosed megaloblastic anemia (Must check B12 levels first to rule out pernicious anemia). **Pregnancy** Category A. Mandatory requirement. Key Risks Neurological: Can mask Vitamin B12 deficiency. If high-dose folate is given to a B12-deficient patient, the anemia improves, but the irreversible neurological damage (subacute combined degeneration of the cord) silently accelerates. Systemic: Extremely benign profile. Virtually zero toxicity as excess is peed out. Key Interactions Methotrexate. Folate replaces the exact compound Methotrexate is trying to starve the body of. If taken on the *same day*, the Folate will cancel out the Methotrexate, causing a severe arthritis flare. Must be staggered. Phenytoin and Barbiturates lower folate levels, and paradoxically, giving folate can lower Phenytoin levels, risking seizures. Monitoring Always check both Serum Folate AND Vitamin B12 levels together before initiating treatment. Monitor **FBC**. Clinical Pearl Women taking Valproate or Carbamazepine for epilepsy are at a massively increased risk of having a baby with spina bifida (due to folate depletion). They MUST be on the high-dose 5 mg folic acid tablet, not the standard 0.5 mg pregnancy multivitamin.","sourceRole":"clinical_reference","access":"public","validationStatus":"unverified","sourceStatus":"current","sourceLineage":[],"publicationVersion":"8dfafee179d5f9599a22a2805ae269529401e254c57cae30396cf5c8519065d7","contentHash":"709100f67e99d9cae38b211c9c01e5b36fad7f2ce175a22dfc7bdc1546b7e5c1"},"renderPayload":{"slug":"folic-acid","name":"Folic acid","class":"Vitamin","subclass":"Water-Soluble (B9)","category":"Vitamins & Minerals","accent":"#0891b2","tag":"VITAMIN","schedule":"