< 30. Also used heavily in palliative care for SC syringe drivers due to high solubility (small volume required). Contraindications & Populations contra Absolute CRITICAL — Severe respiratory depression, asthma attack. Pregnancy CAUTION — **Pregnancy** Category C. Key Interactions inter Pharmacodynamic CRITICAL — Benzodiazepines, CNS depressants. Monitoring & Cautions mon Bedside MANDATORY — Strict monitoring of **SpO2**, **RR**, and Sedation Score. Bedside MANDATORY — Double-check the ampoule concentration. The 'HP' (High Potency) ampoule is 10mg/mL. Giving 1mL of this to a naive patient is equivalent to 50-70mg of IV Morphine and will kill them instantly. Clinical Pearls pearl The Renal Savior If an elderly patient with a fractured NOF has an eGFR of 15, Morphine will give them seizures, and Oxycodone will accumulate. Hydromorphone is clean and safe, making it the definitive choice in nephrology/geriatrics. No Itch If a patient gets terrible hives or itching from IV Morphine, switch them to Hydromorphone. It triggers virtually zero histamine release. Mechanism & Pharmacokinetics evid Mechanism Potent mu-opioid receptor agonist. Lacks the severe histamine-releasing properties of morphine (less itching and hypotension). Onset **IV** 5 mins. **PO** 30 mins. Duration 3-5 h. Half-life 2-3 hours. Metabolised in the liver to Hydromorphone-3-glucuronide (inactive, no neurotoxicity!). Sources src Source Review Source Check - HYDROMORPHONE JUNO-XHP ARTG/PI and PBS search checked 2026-05-13 for high-risk opioid/general batch appraisal: identity/access, indication, dosing, contraindications/populations, interactions, monitoring, pregnancy/lactation, patient-context metadata, and source-row status.\nClass & Role Strong Opioid — Highly potent, pure mu-opioid agonist. Route / Formulation Tablets (2 mg, 4 mg, 8 mg). Oral liquid (1 mg/mL). (Dilaudid, Jurnista (SR)) Usual Dose & Max **PO** 1-2 mg q4-6h PRN. OR **IV** 0.2 - 0.5 mg STAT. Titrated to effect. Key Indication Doses Acute