 & Use ind Primary Hospital-acquired pneumonia, complicated intra-abdominal sepsis, febrile neutropenia, diabetic foot infections. Clinical Place The definitive 'big gun' empiric beta-lactam on the ward. Tightly restricted by antimicrobial stewardship. Contraindications & Populations contra Absolute CRITICAL — Severe penicillin allergy. Cardiovascular CAUTION — Congestive heart failure (due to high sodium load). Pregnancy SAFE — **Pregnancy** Category B1. Key Interactions inter Pharmacodynamic CRITICAL — Vancomycin. The combination 'Vanc/Taz' is notoriously nephrotoxic. Monitor creatinine daily. Pharmacokinetic HIGH — Methotrexate (decreases clearance, risking fatal MTX toxicity). Monitoring & Cautions mon Laboratory MANDATORY — Daily **U&E** and **eGFR** to track renal function. Check **FBC** weekly for bone marrow suppression. Bedside Monitor fluid balance and signs of fluid overload in cardiac patients. Clinical Pearls pearl The Sodium Trap Each 4.5g vial of Tazocin contains ~9.4 mmol of sodium. A patient on q6h dosing receives nearly a liter of Normal Saline's worth of pure sodium every day, which can easily tip an elderly patient into acute pulmonary oedema. Extended Infusions Because beta-lactams depend on 'time above MIC', running a 4.5g dose slowly over 4 hours (extended infusion) provides vastly superior bacterial killing in severe sepsis compared to a 30-minute bolus. Mechanism & Pharmacokinetics evid Mechanism Piperacillin halts cell wall synthesis. Tazobactam irreversibly inhibits beta-lactamases, protecting piperacillin. Excellent tissue penetration. Onset **IV** Immediate. Half-life 1 hour (Short half-life requires extended infusions or frequent dosing for efficacy). Sources src Source Review Source Check - PIPERACILLIN/TAZOBACTAM KABI ARTG/PI and PBS check checked 2026-05-13 for high-risk opioid/general batch appraisal: identity/access, indication, dosing, contraindications/populations, interactions, monitoring, pregnancy/lactation, patient-context me