ive for neuropathic pain, generalised anxiety, and fibromyalgia, but is now Schedule 8 due to high misuse and dependence potential and causes significant dizziness and weight gain. Avoid / Cautions History of severe substance abuse (unless strictly monitored). Severe renal failure without dose adjustment. **Pregnancy** Category B3. Key Risks Neurological: Euphoria, high addiction/abuse potential. HIGH — Dizziness, severe somnolence, ataxia, withdrawal syndrome if stopped abruptly. Respiratory: Synergistic respiratory depression with opioids. Metabolic: Significant weight gain, peripheral edema. Key Interactions Opioids, Benzodiazepines, Alcohol. The combination causes profound respiratory arrest and is the leading cause of poly-drug overdose deaths globally. Monitoring Look for 'lost scripts' or patients demanding early refills. Do not prescribe 300mg capsules to opioid users unless absolutely clinically necessary. Check **eGFR** to dictate safe dosing limits. Clinical Pearl Unlike Gabapentin (which maxes out its absorption transporters in the gut), Pregabalin absorption is linear and >90% at ANY dose. If you swallow 600mg of Pregabalin, 600mg hits your brain. This makes it vastly more effective, but infinitely more abusable.","sourceRole":"clinical_reference","access":"public","validationStatus":"unverified","sourceStatus":"current","sourceLineage":[],"publicationVersion":"5d34ead3064607b445272e2288d00be0bc06bd0162a9cc9cb9571815cf1d44da","contentHash":"ea51488542eaf1cf3ac161882bab560747feaca059c6066c80b25c6368ef1329"},"renderPayload":{"slug":"pregabalin","name":"Pregabalin","class":"Anxiolytic","subclass":"Alpha-2-delta ligand","category":"Neurology - Anticonvulsants","accent":"#0891b2","tag":"GABAPENTINOID","schedule":"S4","stats":[{"label":"Max Dose","value":"600 mg/day","cls":"hi","flag":"hi"},{"label":"Half-life","value":"6 h","cls":"","flag":""},{"label":"Misuse Risk","value":"CRITICAL","cls":"hi","flag":"warn"},{"label":"Sedation","value":"COMMON","cls":"warn