Pharmacodynamic HIGH — Antihypertensives (additive hypotension). Monitoring & Cautions mon Laboratory MANDATORY — Serum Prolactin if symptoms develop. Baseline **BSL**, **Lipids**, and **Weight**. Bedside Monitor for rigidity, tremor, or severe restlessness (akathisia). Clinical Pearls pearl The Typical Atypical Risperidone bridges the gap between old and new antipsychotics. If you prescribe 6-8 mg of Risperidone, you are essentially prescribing Haloperidol. The patient will almost certainly require Benzatropine to counteract the severe stiffness. The Liquid Trap Risperidone oral liquid is incompatible with tea and cola (it precipitates). It must be mixed with water, orange juice, or milk. Mechanism & Pharmacokinetics evid Mechanism Very tight binding to D2 (dopamine) and 5-HT2A (serotonin) receptors. Also blocks alpha-1 receptors (hypotension). Onset **PO** 1-2 hours. Half-life 20 hours (Active metabolite is paliperidone). Metabolised by CYP2D6. Sources src Source Review Source Check - RISPERDAL ARTG/PI and PBS search checked 2026-05-10 for antipsychotic/LAI batch appraisal: identity/access, indication, dosing, contraindications/populations, interactions, monitoring, patient-context metadata, and source-row status.\nClass & Role SGA / Benzisoxazole — Potent D2 and 5-HT2A antagonist. Route / Formulation Tablets (0.5 to 4 mg), ODT Wafers, Oral Liquid (1 mg/mL). (Risperdal, Risperdal Consta (LAI)) Usual Dose & Max **PO** 1 mg **BD** initially. Titrate to target 4-6 mg/day. Max **8 mg/day** (Doses > 6 mg carry severe EPS risks with minimal extra benefit). Key Indication Doses Schizophrenia / Bipolar: **PO** 1 mg **BD** initially. Titrate to target 4-6 mg/day. BPSD (Dementia Agitation): **PO** 0.25 - 0.5 mg **BD**. Max **2 mg/day** in elderly/BPSD. Short-term use only. Renal Impairment: Halve the starting dose if **eGFR** < 30. Best Uses Risperidone is a potent D2/5-HT2A antagonist effective for psychosis and behavioural disturbance, but causes dose-dependent hyperprola