ose Threshold If you prescribe 75mg of Venlafaxine, you are effectively just prescribing a highly toxic, hard-to-stop SSRI. You MUST push the dose to 150mg or 225mg to actually unlock the noradrenaline (SNRI) benefits. The Brain Zaps Venlafaxine has one of the shortest half-lives in psychiatry. If a patient takes their pill at 8 AM, and forgets the next day, by 12 PM they will feel 'electric shocks' in their head and severe vertigo. Counsel heavily on strict adherence. Mechanism & Pharmacokinetics evid Mechanism At 75 mg, it acts almost exclusively as an SSRI. At 150-225 mg, it strongly inhibits Noradrenaline reuptake. At >225 mg, it begins to weakly inhibit Dopamine reuptake. Onset 2-6 WEEKS. Half-life 5 hours (Parent drug). Active metabolite (desvenlafaxine) has an 11-hour half-life. The XR capsule matrix dictates the 24-hour clinical duration. Sources src Source Review Source Check - EFEXOR-XR Australian PI/CMI and PBS search checked 2026-05-10 for antidepressant batch appraisal: identity/access, indication, dosing, contraindications/populations, interactions, monitoring, patient-context metadata, and source-row status.\nClass & Role SNRI — Serotonin-Noradrenaline Reuptake Inhibitor (SNRI). Route / Formulation Extended Release Capsules (37.5 mg, 75 mg, 150 mg). Do not crush. Patient may see intact ghost capsule in stool. (Efexor-XR, Elaxine PR) Usual Dose & Max Start **PO** 75 mg **OD** (XR capsule). Titrate by 75 mg increments every 2-4 weeks. Max 225 mg/day. Key Indication Doses Depression / GAD / Panic: Start **PO** 75 mg **OD** (XR capsule). Titrate by 75 mg increments every 2-4 weeks. Max 225 mg/day. Severe Anxiety / Frail: Start **PO** 37.5 mg **OD** (XR capsule) for the first week to blunt intense initial anxiety/nausea. Best Uses Venlafaxine XR is a potent SNRI for depression, GAD, and neuropathic pain, but causes dose-dependent hypertension requiring BP monitoring and has a severe discontinuation syndrome if stopped abruptly. Avoid / Cautions Concurrent MAOI use (Fatal Serotonin Syndrome), uncontrolled severe hypertension. **Pregnancy** Category B2. Can cause severe withdrawal symptoms in the neonate if used until term. Key Risks Neurological: Discontinuation syndrome ('Brain zaps', dizziness, sensory disturbances, crying spells). HIGH — Insomnia, severe sweating, tremor. Cardiovascular: Dose-dependent hypertension and tachycardia (due to noradrenaline excess). Gastrointestinal: Nausea (severe upon initiation). Key Interactions MAOIs, Tramadol, St John's Wort. Extreme risk of Serotonin Syndrome. NSAIDs (Bleeding risk). Monitoring Baseline and routine **BP** and **HR** checks. If a patient develops hypertension > 150/90, reduce the dose or cease. Routine **U&E** (sodium) for SIADH risk. Clinical Pearl If you prescribe 75mg of Venlafaxine, you are effectively just prescribing a highly toxic, hard-to-stop SSRI. You MUST push the dose to 150mg or 225mg to actually unlock the noradrenaline (SNRI) benefits.","sourceRole":"clinical_reference","access":"public","validationStatus":"unverified","sourceStatus":"current","sourceLineage":[],"publicationVersion":"0fdf219f591999e41c81d5b5c8e9983b19b2fd1aae14ccfd054b847201240a75","contentHash":"7d749acfc8b097a07b2de6c89e4f404abf0fc7bb6e102ff26f39692ec1331967"},"renderPayload":{"slug":"venlafaxine-xr","name":"Venlafaxine XR","class":"Antidepressant","subclass":"SNRI","category":"Psychiatry - Antidepressants","accent":"#7c3aed","tag":"SNRI","schedule":"S4","stats":[{"label":"Max Dose","value":"225 mg/day","cls":"hi","flag":"hi"},{"label":"Half-life","value":"5 h (Act: 11h)","cls":"","flag":""},{"label":"Hypertension","value":"DOSE-DEP","cls":"warn","flag":"warn"},{"label":"Withdrawal","value":"SEVERE","cls":"hi","flag":"warn"}],"sections":[{"title":"Rapid Summary","type":"summary","rows":[{"key":"Overview","val":"Serotonin-Noradrenaline Reuptake Inhibitor (SNRI). Highly effective for severe/refractory depression. The noradrenaline blockade kicks in at higher doses, providing an acti