he Gender Divide The FDA and TGA mandate a 5mg starting dose for women because they clear Zolpidem significantly slower than men. A 10mg dose in a woman often leaves blood levels high enough the next morning to cause car crashes. The Hallucination Trap If a patient takes Zolpidem and fights the sleep to stay awake and watch TV, the drug causes intense, vivid, and often frightening visual hallucinations. They must take it *in bed*. Mechanism & Pharmacokinetics evid Mechanism Binds highly selectively to the alpha-1 subunit of the GABA-A receptor. Induces sleep without significantly altering sleep architecture (maintains deep sleep better than benzos). Has very weak anti-anxiety or muscle-relaxant properties. Onset **PO** 15-30 mins (Must be in bed when taking it). Duration 4-6 h. Half-life 2.5 hours. Cleared by CYP3A4. Sources src Source Review Source Check - ZOLPIDEM-WGR ARTG/PI and PBS search checked 2026-05-12 for sedative/acute-calming batch appraisal: identity/access, indication, dosing, contraindications/populations, interactions, monitoring, pregnancy/lactation, patient-context metadata, and source-row status.\nClass & Role Imidazopyridine / Z-Drug — Non-benzodiazepine 'Z-Drug' hypnotic. Route / Formulation Tablets (10 mg). CR Tablets (12.5 mg - Stilnox CR). (Stilnox, Somidem) Usual Dose & Max **PO** 10 mg STAT immediately before bed. Do not re-dose in the middle of the night. Max **10 mg/day** (Adults) or **5 mg/day** (Elderly / Females). Key Indication Doses Insomnia (Sleep Onset): **PO** 10 mg STAT immediately before bed. Do not re-dose in the middle of the night. Elderly / Females / Hepatic: Max **5 mg/day**. Females clear the drug much slower than males, leaving them impaired the next morning if given 10mg. Best Uses Zolpidem is a Z-drug hypnotic for short-term insomnia management, but causes complex sleep behaviours (sleep-driving, sleep-eating) and should only be used for 2-4 weeks maximum. Avoid / Cautions History of complex sleep behaviors after taking