on's disease. Severe CNS depression/intoxication. Pregnancy CAUTION — **Pregnancy** Category C. Key Interactions inter Pharmacodynamic CRITICAL — High-dose Benzodiazepines. Giving Acuphase to a patient already loaded with Midazolam/Diazepam carries a severe risk of respiratory arrest over the next 24 hours. Monitoring & Cautions mon Bedside MANDATORY — The patient will likely sleep for 2 days. You MUST monitor their **SpO2**, **RR**, and ensure they wake up enough to drink water to prevent severe dehydration and VTE risk from immobility. Clinical Pearls pearl The 3-Day Window Acuphase is the perfect tool for a psychotic patient refusing medications. One injection buys the team exactly 3 days of calm to legally organize treatment orders, establish oral medication regimens, or initiate a 4-weekly depot without fighting the patient every 6 hours for pills. Never Give IV Like all oil-based depots, IV administration will cause fatal pulmonary oil microembolism. Mechanism & Pharmacokinetics evid Mechanism Esterification with acetic acid makes it last 3 days (unlike decanoic acid which lasts 4 weeks). Potent D2, Alpha-1, and H1 blockade. Onset **IM** 2-4 hours. (Peak sedation at 12-24 hours). Duration 72 hours (3 Days). Half-life 32 hours (Released from the oil matrix). Sources src Source Review Source Check - CLOPIXOL ACUPHASE ARTG/PI and PBS search checked 2026-05-10 for antipsychotic/LAI batch appraisal: identity/access, indication, dosing, contraindications/populations, interactions, monitoring, patient-context metadata, and source-row status.\nClass & Role Acuphase (Bridge) — The 'Bridge' depot. Route / Formulation Ampoules (50 mg/1 mL). Viscous oil. (Clopixol Acuphase) Usual Dose & Max **IM** 50-150 mg STAT. May repeat in 2-3 days if necessary. Maximum 4 injections (or 400mg total) per acute episode. Max **400 mg per course** (Max 4 injections total). Key Indication Doses Acute Psychosis / Mania: **IM** 50-150 mg STAT. May repeat in 2-3 days if necessary. Maximum 4 injections (or 400mg total) per acute episode. Elderly / Frail: Max 25-50 mg STAT. Extremely sensitive. Best Uses Zuclopenthixol acetate is a short-acting IM antipsychotic for acute psychosis and severe agitation, but the 72-hour duration means side effects cannot be quickly reversed once administered. Avoid / Cautions Maintenance therapy. Parkinson's disease. Severe CNS depression/intoxication. **Pregnancy** Category C. Key Risks Neurological: Extreme, unavoidable sedation for 2-3 days. HIGH — EPS, dystonia. Cardiovascular: Hypotension, tachycardia. Gastrointestinal: Dry mouth, constipation. Key Interactions High-dose Benzodiazepines. Giving Acuphase to a patient already loaded with Midazolam/Diazepam carries a severe risk of respiratory arrest over the next 24 hours. Monitoring The patient will likely sleep for 2 days. You MUST monitor their **SpO2**, **RR**, and ensure they wake up enough to drink water to prevent severe dehydration and VTE risk from immobility. Clinical Pearl Acuphase is the perfect tool for a psychotic patient refusing medications. One injection buys the team exactly 3 days of calm to legally organize treatment orders, establish oral medication regimens, or initiate a 4-weekly depot without fighting the patient every 6 hours for pills.","sourceRole":"clinical_reference","access":"public","validationStatus":"unverified","sourceStatus":"current","sourceLineage":[],"publicationVersion":"110dab7640d0bf87ec0a777a9dcda031103d587c00227078c0768596fbfc84af","contentHash":"1f78883f86922d90ddfdf818b06c60bb56878884b5d0d11fcd45172f1dcfb4c8"},"renderPayload":{"slug":"zuclopenthixol-acetate","name":"Zuclopenthixol acetate","class":"Antipsychotic","subclass":"Acuphase (Bridge)","category":"Psychiatry - Depot Antipsychotics","accent":"#0d9488","tag":"72H BRIDGE","schedule":"S4","stats":[{"label":"Max Dose","value":"400 mg / 4 INJECTIONS","cls":"hi","flag":"hi"},{"label":"Duration","value":"72 HOURS","cls":"good","flag":""},{"label":"Sedation","value":"CRITICAL",