cardiovascular disease, acute severe CNS depression. Pregnancy CAUTION — **Pregnancy** Category C. Key Interactions inter Pharmacodynamic CRITICAL — Synergistic respiratory depression with high-dose Benzodiazepines or Opioids. Pharmacodynamic HIGH — Antihypertensives (Additive hypotension). Monitoring & Cautions mon Bedside MANDATORY — Monitor for over-sedation and falls, especially in the 3-4 days immediately following the injection. Laboratory Baseline **ECG**, **Lipids**, and **Weight**. Clinical Pearls pearl The Calming Anchor While modern psychiatry prefers non-sedating drugs (like Aripiprazole), Zuclopenthixol Depot remains essential in forensic or high-acuity wards where the patient's baseline aggression poses a physical danger to staff and themselves. Viscous Oil Because the suspension is so thick, it must be drawn up with a large-bore needle and injected slowly deep into the glute. Rapid pushing causes severe muscle trauma. Mechanism & Pharmacokinetics evid Mechanism Thioxanthene derivative. Potent D2 antagonist. High affinity for Alpha-1 and H1 receptors (driving the intense sedation and calming effect). Onset Days. Steady state takes months. Half-life 17 Days (Released slowly from the oil depot). Sources src Source Review Source Check - CLOPIXOL DEPOT ARTG/PI and PBS search checked 2026-05-10 for antipsychotic/LAI batch appraisal: identity/access, indication, dosing, contraindications/populations, interactions, monitoring, patient-context metadata, and source-row status.\nClass & Role Clopixol Depot — First-Generation Antipsychotic (FGA) depot in fractionated coconut oil. Route / Formulation Ampoules (200 mg/1 mL). Thick oil solution. (Clopixol Depot) Usual Dose & Max **IM** 200-400 mg every 2 to 4 weeks. Deep gluteal Z-Track injection. Max **600 mg/week** (Though typical doses are 200-400 mg every 2-4 weeks). Key Indication Doses Schizophrenia / Severe Agitation: **IM** 200-400 mg every 2 to 4 weeks. Deep gluteal Z-Track injection. Elderly / Frail: Max 5